8
00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.977
[wailing sound plays]

9
00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:55.091
[♪ enchanting music playing]

10
00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:02.473
Star.

11
00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:07.645
Comm... Command.

12
00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:12.442
Star.

13
00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:14.194
Command.

14
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.447
[all] Star. Command.

15
00:03:17.488 --> 00:03:18.823
-Rendezvous!
-With!

16
00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:19.991
[all] Star Command.

17
00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.410
Rendezvous with Star Command.

18
00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:24.704
Rendezvous with Star Command.

19
00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:26.706
Rendezvous with Star Command.

20
00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:29.042
Rendezvous with Star Command.

21
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:31.419
Rendezvous with Star Command.

22
00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:33.963
Rendezvous with Star Command.

23
00:03:34.005 --> 00:03:36.299
Rendezvous with Star Command.

24
00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:38.343
Rendezvous with Star Command.

25
00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:01.157
There.

26
00:04:03.201 --> 00:04:06.246
This way.
you'll never lose me. Jessie.

27
00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.208
Friends forever. partner.

28
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.376
[giggles]

29
00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.253
That's right. partner.

30
00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:16.547
But don't you worry.
I'll keep a good eye on you.

31
00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.632
[grunts]

32
00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:22.428
See? I'm still watching.

33
00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.930
[giggles]

34
00:04:23.972 --> 00:04:26.683
I'm gone... [gasps]
...but I'm back.

35
00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:29.769
I'm gone. [gasps] I'm back.

36
00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.230
I still see you.

37
00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.108
[gasps] Oh. no.
[echoing] I'm gone.

38
00:04:37.568 --> 00:04:40.655
And I will love you
all the time...

39
00:04:40.697 --> 00:04:44.033
even when I'm mad or sad

40
00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:46.160
or leave you outside
by accident.

41
00:04:46.202 --> 00:04:48.079
I'll still love you forever.

42
00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.498
[as Jessie]
Really? You mean it?

43
00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.208
Forever and ever and ever?

44
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.711
Yep. All the evers.

45
00:04:54.752 --> 00:04:57.714
Then do you. Forky.
take Karen Beverly

46
00:04:57.755 --> 00:05:00.049
to be your beloved bride?

47
00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:01.426
[as Forky] I do.

48
00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.261
And do you. Karen Beverly?

49
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.512
[as Karen Beverly] I do.

50
00:05:04.554 --> 00:05:06.556
[sobs. blows nose]

51
00:05:07.682 --> 00:05:09.100
[giggles]

52
00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:11.144
Yeehaw!

53
00:05:11.185 --> 00:05:13.604
I now pronounce you husband...

54
00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.732
and knife.

55
00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.192
[kissing]

56
00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.819
Kissy. kissy.

57
00:05:19.861 --> 00:05:22.155
-[kissing continues]
-[gasps]

58
00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:23.698
[chuckles]

59
00:05:25.408 --> 00:05:28.244
[gasps] Who poisoned
the maid of honor?

60
00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:29.370
[shouts. groans]

61
00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:31.247
-[shouts]
-[all gasp]

62
00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:32.707
-[gasps]
-[screaming]

63
00:05:32.749 --> 00:05:38.212
Oh! Why? Why?

64
00:05:38.254 --> 00:05:39.422
Everyone!

65
00:05:40.089 --> 00:05:42.800
Step aside. I know CPR.

66
00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.469
One. two. three.

67
00:05:45.094 --> 00:05:48.306
Now. the kiss of life.

68
00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:49.349
[gasps]

69
00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.392
[inhales deeply. blows]

70
00:05:55.897 --> 00:05:56.939
Oh.

71
00:05:56.981 --> 00:05:58.775
[inhales deeply. blows]

72
00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:01.611
-[inhales deeply]
-[car approaching]

73
00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.655
[child 1 chuckling]

74
00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.657
[child 2] You're so funny.

75
00:06:09.911 --> 00:06:11.954
But we didn't solve my murder.

76
00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:14.207
Just hold your horses. Rex.

77
00:06:14.248 --> 00:06:15.958
Psst. Dolly. what's going on?

78
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.752
[sighs] Not sure.

79
00:06:17.794 --> 00:06:19.128
You know. at first I was mad

80
00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.713
Bonnie drew
these glasses on me.

81
00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:22.340
but honestly. I can see
so much better now.

82
00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.925
Dolly. focus.

83
00:06:23.966 --> 00:06:25.718
Oh! Sorry.

84
00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.220
It's the Jordan twins.
They're back home.

85
00:06:27.261 --> 00:06:30.515
[twins chattering]

86
00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.642
[laughing]

87
00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.979
Poor thing. She's still afraid
to ask them to play.

88
00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.482
Not this time. [grunts]

89
00:06:41.526 --> 00:06:42.610
[chattering continues]

90
00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:43.528
[Jessie grunts]

91
00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:46.823
Giddy-up there!
Time's a-wastin'!

92
00:06:46.864 --> 00:06:48.116
[gasps] Oh. no.

93
00:06:54.163 --> 00:06:55.289
[twins laughing]

94
00:06:58.042 --> 00:06:59.752
That's it. Bonnie.

95
00:06:59.794 --> 00:07:01.087
You can do it.

96
00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:12.974
[Bonnie gasps]

97
00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:17.103
[as Jessie] Hello.

98
00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:21.107
[twins laugh]

99
00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.693
[door closes]

100
00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:32.410
Uh. Jessie.
The wedding got me thinking...

101
00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:33.786
Shh. Something's off.

102
00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:36.080
So. how'd the wedding go?

103
00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.707
Who murdered
the maid of honor this time?

104
00:07:37.748 --> 00:07:39.876
Mom? Dad?

105
00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.210
Yeah. sweetie?

106
00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:45.756
Why won't anyone be my friend?

107
00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.258
[all gasp]

108
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.219
-Oh. Bonnie. come here.
-Oh. sweetie.

109
00:07:55.391 --> 00:07:57.059
-Buzz.
-Ow.

110
00:07:57.101 --> 00:07:58.728
You're deputy till I get back.

111
00:07:58.769 --> 00:08:00.480
Me? Right.

112
00:08:00.521 --> 00:08:03.316
I'm gonna get those twins
to play with Bonnie somehow.

113
00:08:03.357 --> 00:08:04.692
Come on. Bullseye.

114
00:08:06.777 --> 00:08:08.821
[♪ adventurous music playing]

115
00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.209
[♪ ominous music playing]

116
00:08:22.251 --> 00:08:23.336
Huh?

117
00:08:24.462 --> 00:08:27.048
Why. they're... they're both
just sitting there.

118
00:08:28.132 --> 00:08:29.425
Doin' nothing.

119
00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.595
They ain't playing with toys
at all.

120
00:08:32.637 --> 00:08:34.931
What. you didn't hear?

121
00:08:34.972 --> 00:08:36.724
Uh. n-no. I... I didn't hear.

122
00:08:36.766 --> 00:08:38.601
-She didn't hear.
-She didn't hear?

123
00:08:38.643 --> 00:08:40.686
What? What didn't I hear?

124
00:08:40.728 --> 00:08:42.522
The age of toys is over. lass.

125
00:08:42.563 --> 00:08:44.732
What do you mean. "over"?
When did that happen?

126
00:08:44.774 --> 00:08:47.985
It's been happening for years.
Where have you been?

127
00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:50.279
[stammers]
Across the street. playing.

128
00:08:50.321 --> 00:08:51.614
[all] Playing?

129
00:08:51.656 --> 00:08:53.824
Oh! Your kid still plays?

130
00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:56.661
I don't remember play.
Describe it to me.

131
00:08:56.702 --> 00:09:00.039
[stammers] Are you guys okay?
What happened to you?

132
00:09:00.081 --> 00:09:01.999
-[all] Tech!
-Devices!

133
00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.918
Everywhere. devices!

134
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.711
Phones! Tablets!

135
00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:07.255
Computers! Cameras!

136
00:09:07.296 --> 00:09:08.714
The screens just took over!

137
00:09:08.756 --> 00:09:10.883
All the tapping. The tapping!

138
00:09:10.925 --> 00:09:12.760
Tap. tap. tap. tap.

139
00:09:12.802 --> 00:09:14.595
-Make it stop.
-The tapping. Not the tapping!

140
00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:16.138
Take our advice. darlin'.

141
00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:17.932
Find a drawer and hide.

142
00:09:17.974 --> 00:09:19.475
'cause once tech
invades your home.

143
00:09:19.517 --> 00:09:21.143
you're dead where you lie.

144
00:09:21.185 --> 00:09:24.939
[chuckles] Oh. well.
it's probably just a fad.

145
00:09:24.981 --> 00:09:28.067
Like. you know. record players
or Hula-Hoops.

146
00:09:28.109 --> 00:09:29.610
You don't get it.

147
00:09:29.652 --> 00:09:31.862
The age of toys is over.

148
00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:32.989
Over.

149
00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.449
Tap. tap. tap...

150
00:09:35.491 --> 00:09:39.245
Don't believe us?
Come see for yourself.

151
00:09:41.664 --> 00:09:44.083
[Jessie groaning. grunting]

152
00:09:45.293 --> 00:09:47.461
-[grunts. gasps]
-[grunts]

153
00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:50.673
[Jessie] Look at 'em all.

154
00:09:51.882 --> 00:09:54.176
All on devices.

155
00:09:56.804 --> 00:09:58.764
Except for Bonnie.

156
00:09:58.806 --> 00:10:00.349
[sighs]

157
00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:02.268
No wonder she can't
make a friend. Bullseye.

158
00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.605
She's the only one out there
still playing with toys.

159
00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.773
[sighs]

160
00:10:07.815 --> 00:10:10.776
-Don't worry. We're safe.
-[giggles]

161
00:10:13.654 --> 00:10:15.448
Are we sure about this?

162
00:10:15.489 --> 00:10:18.784
[sighs]
No. but I think it might help.

163
00:10:18.826 --> 00:10:20.661
[sighs] Okay.

164
00:10:21.537 --> 00:10:22.413
[phone chimes]

165
00:10:22.913 --> 00:10:24.498
[gasps]

166
00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.168
A Lilypad! Oh. thank you. Mom.
Thank you. Dad.

167
00:10:27.209 --> 00:10:29.837
Well. now that you're eight.
we thought you were ready.

168
00:10:32.048 --> 00:10:34.467
Hi. there. I'm Lilypad.
Welcome to The Pond.

169
00:10:34.508 --> 00:10:36.677
You can take today
to figure out how to use it.

170
00:10:36.719 --> 00:10:38.429
but then tomorrow.
we'll start having

171
00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.389
-strict screen time.
-[Bonnie] Uh-huh.

172
00:10:43.601 --> 00:10:44.644
[Bullseye grunts]

173
00:10:46.896 --> 00:10:49.357
[Lilypad beeping]

174
00:10:50.274 --> 00:10:53.402
[chuckles] Uh-oh. try again.

175
00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:55.988
Keep hopping.

176
00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.698
[frog croaking]

177
00:10:58.783 --> 00:11:00.618
[beeping continues]

178
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.036
Try again.

179
00:11:10.252 --> 00:11:12.713
Morning.
Screen time's over now.

180
00:11:12.755 --> 00:11:14.674
Let's put Lilypad away
and come to breakfast.

181
00:11:14.715 --> 00:11:16.050
Okay.

182
00:11:22.973 --> 00:11:24.809
[Hamm] We can't
let that thing replace us.

183
00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.770
Jumpin' jelly beans!
Will y'all just settle down?

184
00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:30.940
Now. I'm gonna have some words
with this Lilypad

185
00:11:30.981 --> 00:11:33.025
and let her know how
things are run around here.

186
00:11:33.067 --> 00:11:35.486
-Try to stay calm. Jessie.
-Buzz. you know me.

187
00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:37.071
I'm the definition of calm.

188
00:11:37.113 --> 00:11:38.322
-[whinnies]
-[Buzz laughs]

189
00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.573
That's not gonna work.

190
00:11:39.615 --> 00:11:40.574
[grunts]

191
00:11:44.495 --> 00:11:45.663
[Bullseye grunts]

192
00:11:47.164 --> 00:11:48.958
-Hi!
-What the--

193
00:11:48.999 --> 00:11:52.044
Sorry. I didn't mean to scare
you. Sleep mode. you know?

194
00:11:52.086 --> 00:11:53.963
No? Eh. forget it.

195
00:11:54.004 --> 00:11:55.381
I was just gonna
hop on the charger.

196
00:11:55.423 --> 00:11:57.091
Battery could use
a little refresh.

197
00:11:57.133 --> 00:11:59.885
-I wanna talk to you. device.
-Please. call me "Lily."

198
00:11:59.927 --> 00:12:02.388
Now look here. Me and the toys
have been working all summer

199
00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:05.015
to try and get Bonnie to make
friends with the Jordan twins

200
00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:06.600
-across the street.
-Uh-huh. Yeah.

201
00:12:06.642 --> 00:12:08.269
-Then you had to ruin it...
-Got it.

202
00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:09.437
...with all your stupid...

203
00:12:09.478 --> 00:12:10.646
You're not even listening

204
00:12:10.688 --> 00:12:12.148
-to me!
-Oh. no.

205
00:12:12.189 --> 00:12:14.483
I was listening.
I'm always listening. See?

206
00:12:14.525 --> 00:12:16.777
Now look here. Me and the toys
have been working all summer

207
00:12:16.819 --> 00:12:18.487
to try to get Bonnie to make
friends with the Jordan twins.

208
00:12:18.529 --> 00:12:19.822
Now in Spanish.

209
00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:22.074
-[speaking Spanish]
-[all gasp]

210
00:12:22.116 --> 00:12:23.909
-Now as a rap.
-[♪ drumbeat playing]

211
00:12:23.951 --> 00:12:25.786
♪ Me and the toys
Been working all summer ♪

212
00:12:25.828 --> 00:12:26.954
♪ Trying to get Bonnie
To make friends ♪

213
00:12:26.996 --> 00:12:28.164
Ooh! Our first dance. honey!

214
00:12:28.205 --> 00:12:29.707
Oh. this concerns me
ethically.

215
00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:31.876
[♪ drumbeat stops]

216
00:12:31.917 --> 00:12:33.711
Whatever.
You don't understand.

217
00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:35.796
Our kid needs to learn
how to make friends.

218
00:12:35.838 --> 00:12:37.757
and your screen ain't helping.

219
00:12:37.798 --> 00:12:40.176
Look. if it's friends Bonnie
needs. consider it done.

220
00:12:40.217 --> 00:12:42.094
-[chimes]
-There.

221
00:12:42.136 --> 00:12:44.346
What?
[stammers] What happened?

222
00:12:44.388 --> 00:12:46.724
Oh. it was easy. I just
sent a friend request

223
00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.642
to all the girls
in Bonnie's dance class.

224
00:12:48.684 --> 00:12:50.394
But that's...
They're not here.

225
00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:52.813
Oh. yes. they are. silly.

226
00:12:52.855 --> 00:12:55.566
Chelsea. Kara and even Heidi.
they're all here.

227
00:12:55.608 --> 00:12:58.152
The parents created
a group chat on The Pond.

228
00:12:58.194 --> 00:12:59.862
You see. on The Pond.

229
00:12:59.904 --> 00:13:01.405
while Bonnie's playing
my fun learning games.

230
00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:03.282
she can also socialize
with other kids.

231
00:13:03.324 --> 00:13:06.368
That's why Mom and Dad bought
me. To make connections.

232
00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:10.456
-Voila! Friend made.
-[all exclaim]

233
00:13:10.498 --> 00:13:11.957
I want one.

234
00:13:11.999 --> 00:13:14.001
That Lilypad made Bonnie
a friend in. like...

235
00:13:14.043 --> 00:13:15.544
Fifteen seconds.
I was counting.

236
00:13:15.586 --> 00:13:17.505
-What? No.
-No touching.

237
00:13:17.546 --> 00:13:20.299
That ain't a friend. A real
friend would actually be here.

238
00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:21.425
Well. that's my point.
Jessica.

239
00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:22.760
[gasps]

240
00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:24.053
-Oh. no.
-[Hamm] She used the "J" word.

241
00:13:24.094 --> 00:13:25.596
[Rex] Scandal!

242
00:13:25.638 --> 00:13:27.264
With my help.
eventually Bonnie can reach

243
00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:28.808
all of her
developmental goals.

244
00:13:28.849 --> 00:13:30.434
I just want
what's best for her.

245
00:13:30.476 --> 00:13:32.645
I think I know more
than a green calculator

246
00:13:32.686 --> 00:13:33.854
what's best for Bonnie.

247
00:13:33.896 --> 00:13:35.898
-Uh. really?
-Yeah. really.

248
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.900
I got three kids' worth
of know-how.

249
00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:42.530
Bonnie. Before that. Andy.
and before that. Emily.

250
00:13:42.571 --> 00:13:44.615
I think that just means
you're old.

251
00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:47.034
Yikes! Wow. Really old.

252
00:13:47.076 --> 00:13:48.661
Fine. We'll wrestle for her.

253
00:13:48.702 --> 00:13:50.871
-Hi-yah! Come on!
-Whoa! [chuckling]

254
00:13:50.996 --> 00:13:52.498
Wrestle me.
you frog-faced faker.

255
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.083
That kinda tickles.

256
00:13:54.124 --> 00:13:55.793
-I'll knock ya off this bed.
-I thought we were

257
00:13:55.835 --> 00:13:57.461
-staying calm-- Ah!
-Put up a fight. you riffraff.

258
00:13:57.503 --> 00:13:58.796
-Whoa!
-I'll show you who's better

259
00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:00.172
-for Bonnie.
-Okay.

260
00:14:00.214 --> 00:14:01.549
Nobody said anything
about lifting.

261
00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:03.384
-[Dad] Bonnie?
-[Bonnie] Just a sec.

262
00:14:13.477 --> 00:14:14.895
-[Bonnie screams]
-[coughs]

263
00:14:14.937 --> 00:14:16.105
-Mom! Dad!
-Bonnie?

264
00:14:16.146 --> 00:14:17.481
What? [stammers] What's wrong?

265
00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:18.858
Chelsea from dance class

266
00:14:18.983 --> 00:14:20.067
invited me to a sleepover
this weekend.

267
00:14:20.109 --> 00:14:22.027
Can I go? Can I go? Can I go?

268
00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.196
Please!

269
00:14:24.238 --> 00:14:26.031
Well. uh. all right.

270
00:14:26.073 --> 00:14:29.076
As long as we talk
to Chelsea's parents.

271
00:14:29.118 --> 00:14:30.411
I guess it's okay.

272
00:14:30.452 --> 00:14:32.538
Yay! Yes!

273
00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.456
[Dad]
Come on. everybody. Let's eat.

274
00:14:37.835 --> 00:14:39.920
Yeah. I got dibs on
behind the dresser.

275
00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:41.171
Should buy me a few years.

276
00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:43.549
Ah! Extinction. Not again.

277
00:14:43.591 --> 00:14:45.467
-Called it.
-Don't get me started.

278
00:14:45.509 --> 00:14:48.345
Now. look. Our time ain't over
yet. Bonnie still loves us.

279
00:14:48.387 --> 00:14:49.972
-[Dolly] Really?
-[Jessie] She does.

280
00:14:50.014 --> 00:14:52.600
Sure.
Whatever you say. Sheriff.

281
00:14:54.435 --> 00:14:56.103
It's just a phase.

282
00:14:58.314 --> 00:14:59.607
[sighs]

283
00:14:59.648 --> 00:15:01.692
[♪ sentimental music playing]

284
00:15:12.828 --> 00:15:14.788
[♪ marching music playing]

285
00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:28.177
[static crackling]

286
00:15:29.845 --> 00:15:30.888
[sighs]

287
00:15:32.097 --> 00:15:35.225
[beeping]

288
00:15:35.267 --> 00:15:37.269
'Ello? Caboom here. Over.

289
00:15:37.311 --> 00:15:39.855
-[Jessie] Oh! Duke.
-Hey there. Red.

290
00:15:39.897 --> 00:15:41.982
-Long time.
- Hey. Um...

291
00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:43.901
- Is Woody there?
-Please hold.

292
00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.282
[exclaims] Hey. cowboy!

293
00:15:50.324 --> 00:15:52.034
Pump the brakes. Duke.
he's mid-rescue.

294
00:15:52.076 --> 00:15:54.244
Bad squirrel! No! Yeah. bad!

295
00:15:54.286 --> 00:15:56.664
-Evil squirrel! No!
-Okay. now. Mr. Nutcase.

296
00:15:56.705 --> 00:15:59.249
-Doctor. Doctor.
-Okay. Dr. Nutcase.

297
00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:02.211
On three. you're going to
unstick yourself

298
00:16:02.252 --> 00:16:03.712
-and drop into my arms.
-[sobbing]

299
00:16:03.754 --> 00:16:06.548
What's the point?
It's over for toys.

300
00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:09.969
The screens have won. and now
the squirrel's gonna eat me!

301
00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.303
You guys ready?

302
00:16:11.345 --> 00:16:13.013
Just one text. ping.

303
00:16:13.055 --> 00:16:14.974
and Trevor totally forgot
I was stuck in the tree.

304
00:16:15.015 --> 00:16:16.350
[crying] We're doomed!

305
00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:20.145
Okay. one. two...

306
00:16:20.187 --> 00:16:21.355
I give up!

307
00:16:21.397 --> 00:16:22.690
[shouts] Three. three!

308
00:16:25.025 --> 00:16:26.360
I got you. I got you.

309
00:16:26.402 --> 00:16:28.237
[Dr. Nutcase sobbing]

310
00:16:28.278 --> 00:16:31.740
-Okay. It's okay. I got you.
-Let me go! I'm yucky.

311
00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:35.744
-[Woody] Hello. Jessie? Hello?
-[gasps] Woody!

312
00:16:35.786 --> 00:16:37.496
Jessie. hey. What's going on?

313
00:16:37.538 --> 00:16:39.373
-Curse technology!
-Hey. quiet down.

314
00:16:39.415 --> 00:16:41.625
[Dr. Nutcase]
We're all just landfill now.

315
00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:44.920
Woody. is it as bad out there
for toys as they say it is?

316
00:16:44.962 --> 00:16:46.755
-Beware the machines!
-Just let go!

317
00:16:46.797 --> 00:16:48.465
Yeah. Yeah. it's bad.

318
00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:50.551
We're finding
more abandoned toys each day.

319
00:16:50.592 --> 00:16:52.094
Why? Are you guys okay?

320
00:16:52.136 --> 00:16:55.806
Not really.
Tech's invaded our house too.

321
00:16:55.848 --> 00:16:56.724
[Woody] Oh. no.

322
00:16:56.765 --> 00:16:58.392
Yeah. her name's Lilypad.

323
00:16:58.517 --> 00:17:01.103
Looks like a frog.
but really. she's a leech.

324
00:17:01.145 --> 00:17:03.313
sucking up
all of Bonnie's attention.

325
00:17:03.397 --> 00:17:06.608
Making her stare
at her screen all day.

326
00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:09.069
There's got to be
some way to stop it.

327
00:17:09.111 --> 00:17:11.113
[stammers]
I don't know. Jessie. Uh...

328
00:17:11.155 --> 00:17:14.158
Toys are for play.
but tech is...

329
00:17:14.241 --> 00:17:16.493
it's for everything.

330
00:17:16.535 --> 00:17:17.661
[sighs]

331
00:17:19.121 --> 00:17:22.041
You remember
my first kid. Emily?

332
00:17:22.082 --> 00:17:25.586
The one I told you about
who gave me away.

333
00:17:25.627 --> 00:17:27.379
[Woody] Course I do. yeah.

334
00:17:27.421 --> 00:17:30.215
It feels like that
all over again.

335
00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:32.926
First we were playing...

336
00:17:32.968 --> 00:17:34.636
[Emily laughs]

337
00:17:34.678 --> 00:17:36.055
...and then the world
started changing.

338
00:17:36.096 --> 00:17:38.223
[laughs] I know.

339
00:17:38.265 --> 00:17:40.350
[Jessie]
Emily changed and then...

340
00:17:41.268 --> 00:17:42.352
just like that...

341
00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.564
my time with her was over.

342
00:17:47.024 --> 00:17:50.319
Now I'm losing Bonnie
to this device.

343
00:17:51.653 --> 00:17:53.572
Is it me?

344
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:56.200
Am I just no good
at being a toy?

345
00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:58.202
[Woody]
Jessie. you're a good toy.

346
00:17:58.243 --> 00:18:00.579
-I don't know.
-[Woody] Jessie.

347
00:18:02.831 --> 00:18:03.707
[Bullseye grunts]

348
00:18:04.958 --> 00:18:07.753
[inhales sharply] Okay.
Jessie... [clears throat]

349
00:18:07.795 --> 00:18:10.798
No. Sheriff... Sheriff Jessie.
I appreciate this promotion.

350
00:18:10.839 --> 00:18:12.674
but what I'd really like
to promote...

351
00:18:12.716 --> 00:18:14.510
No. that is so stupid.

352
00:18:14.593 --> 00:18:16.678
[Bullseye sniffing]

353
00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.723
But she got Bonnie invited
to a sleepover in seconds.

354
00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:22.893
[Woody] Jessie. you know
Bonnie better than anyone.

355
00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:24.478
What does your gut say?

356
00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:32.736
-That it can't be that easy.
-[Woody] Mm-hmm.

357
00:18:32.778 --> 00:18:33.987
Bonnie won't click

358
00:18:34.029 --> 00:18:35.489
-with just anyone.
- Exactly.

359
00:18:35.531 --> 00:18:37.866
She needs to actually
meet these girls.

360
00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:41.662
She's not like most kids.
Bonnie plays different. She...

361
00:18:43.872 --> 00:18:45.833
She needs to play.

362
00:18:45.874 --> 00:18:47.835
-[Woody] Jessie?
-You're right. Woody.

363
00:18:47.876 --> 00:18:49.545
Toys are for play.

364
00:18:49.586 --> 00:18:52.047
And play is how
she'll find the right friend.

365
00:18:52.089 --> 00:18:53.173
Okay.

366
00:18:53.215 --> 00:18:55.300
The age of toys may be over.

367
00:18:55.342 --> 00:18:58.303
but I'm gonna do something
useful before I go.

368
00:18:58.345 --> 00:18:59.805
I'm going to that sleepover.

369
00:18:59.847 --> 00:19:02.683
and making a real friend
for Bonnie.

370
00:19:02.724 --> 00:19:04.643
-Jessie. are you okay?
-[gasps] Buzz!

371
00:19:04.685 --> 00:19:06.186
-Jessie? Jessie!
-[static on radio]

372
00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:07.896
What do you think
you're doing?

373
00:19:07.938 --> 00:19:09.731
What are you doing?
I assumed you needed backup.

374
00:19:09.773 --> 00:19:10.941
No! I don't...

375
00:19:10.983 --> 00:19:13.694
Need backup. Deputy.

376
00:19:13.735 --> 00:19:15.279
[gasps]

377
00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.406
-[whispers] What happened?
-Why are we whispering?

378
00:19:17.447 --> 00:19:18.574
-He's finally asleep.
-[snoring]

379
00:19:18.615 --> 00:19:20.033
So what's wrong?

380
00:19:20.075 --> 00:19:21.994
I don't know.
but you heard Jessie.

381
00:19:22.035 --> 00:19:23.704
She needs a deputy.

382
00:19:23.745 --> 00:19:24.830
[screams] Machines!

383
00:19:24.872 --> 00:19:26.790
-Jessie.
-Yeah. what is it?

384
00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:27.875
Uh...

385
00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.753
[stammers] You know...
Never mind. Never mind.

386
00:19:31.795 --> 00:19:33.964
If you need anything.
I'm here. At your service.

387
00:19:34.006 --> 00:19:36.091
Okay. Thanks.

388
00:19:36.133 --> 00:19:38.594
Come on. Bullseye.
I'm gonna need your help.

389
00:19:38.635 --> 00:19:40.012
[Bullseye whinnies]

390
00:19:40.053 --> 00:19:41.388
[Buzz sighs]

391
00:19:46.643 --> 00:19:49.229
[♪ adventurous music playing]

392
00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:02.284
We can't see the stars. Buzz.
Too much fog.

393
00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:06.121
Hmm.
We need to find higher ground.

394
00:20:06.163 --> 00:20:08.749
-[gasps]
-[all beeping]

395
00:20:17.299 --> 00:20:19.343
[♪ dramatic music playing]

396
00:20:36.944 --> 00:20:38.028
[machinery whirring]

397
00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:39.112
Huh?

398
00:20:49.331 --> 00:20:50.374
A-ha!

399
00:20:59.675 --> 00:21:02.302
Buzz. I have our bearings.
East-north-- [gasps]

400
00:21:10.644 --> 00:21:12.396
I'm not cleaning that up.

401
00:21:16.024 --> 00:21:18.527
-Why did we...
-Freeze?

402
00:21:19.069 --> 00:21:20.028
[all] Fascinating.

403
00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:21.446
-Must...
-Avoid...

404
00:21:21.488 --> 00:21:22.364
Humans.

405
00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:23.615
[all] Affirmative.

406
00:21:23.657 --> 00:21:26.159
[♪ dramatic music plays]

407
00:21:29.955 --> 00:21:31.290
[music fades]

408
00:21:31.331 --> 00:21:33.083
Bonnie! Time to go
to your sleepover.

409
00:21:34.334 --> 00:21:35.252
Hmm.

410
00:21:37.087 --> 00:21:38.380
Um...

411
00:21:40.215 --> 00:21:42.676
Yo. Bonnie.
uh. what are you doing?

412
00:21:42.718 --> 00:21:44.553
You said you finished packing.

413
00:21:44.594 --> 00:21:47.306
Well. I did. but it's
my very first sleepover. Dad.

414
00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:49.349
I wanna be
extra. extra prepared.

415
00:21:49.391 --> 00:21:50.976
You're gonna be fine. sweetie.

416
00:21:51.018 --> 00:21:53.228
Come on. Go put on your shoes.
We got to go.

417
00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.354
Okay. okay.

418
00:21:58.942 --> 00:21:59.985
[clears throat]

419
00:22:00.027 --> 00:22:01.111
Jessie. [gasps]

420
00:22:02.821 --> 00:22:03.822
[Lilypad] Uh...

421
00:22:04.406 --> 00:22:06.074
What are you doing?

422
00:22:06.116 --> 00:22:09.536
We are gonna check out
these "friends" for ourselves

423
00:22:09.578 --> 00:22:11.872
and see if there is a real one
in the bunch.

424
00:22:11.913 --> 00:22:13.832
Okay. pause. It is not
a good look for Bonnie

425
00:22:13.874 --> 00:22:15.834
-to bring toys to a sleepover.
-[scoffs]

426
00:22:15.876 --> 00:22:17.169
-I do. I do. I do.
-Deputy Buzz.

427
00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:19.588
I do!
I mean. I've done things.

428
00:22:19.629 --> 00:22:21.506
Make sure that device
don't take charge of anything

429
00:22:21.548 --> 00:22:22.507
while we're away.

430
00:22:22.549 --> 00:22:24.134
Yes. Sheriff. I'm on it.

431
00:22:24.176 --> 00:22:26.011
-[Dad] All right. time to go.
-[Bonnie] Okay.

432
00:22:26.053 --> 00:22:27.846
No. Jessie.
Get out of that bag.

433
00:22:27.888 --> 00:22:29.848
I'm only thinking about
what's best for Bonnie.

434
00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.768
Well. what do you know?
That's exactly what I'm doing.

435
00:22:38.565 --> 00:22:40.942
-[door closes]
-[car rumbling]

436
00:22:40.984 --> 00:22:42.527
[Dad]
Did you pack your toothbrush?

437
00:22:42.569 --> 00:22:44.237
-[Bonnie] I think so.
-[zipper opens]

438
00:22:45.697 --> 00:22:48.742
Oh. thanks. Dad. You packed
Jessie and Bullseye.

439
00:22:48.784 --> 00:22:51.536
Uh. did I?
Well. you're welcome.

440
00:22:51.578 --> 00:22:52.829
[Bonnie sighs]

441
00:22:52.871 --> 00:22:54.664
-And here we are.
-[gasps]

442
00:22:55.332 --> 00:22:56.875
Oh. oh. oh. oh!

443
00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:59.711
I wonder if Kara and Heidi
are here yet.

444
00:22:59.753 --> 00:23:02.422
Oh! Over there. Dad.
I see them. Park right there.

445
00:23:02.464 --> 00:23:04.424
[Dad] Okay. okay. I see them.

446
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:08.053
Uh. Bonnie.
You forgot your bag.

447
00:23:08.095 --> 00:23:09.346
[panting]

448
00:23:09.388 --> 00:23:11.640
-Hey. Chelsea.
-Oh. hey. Bonnie.

449
00:23:11.681 --> 00:23:13.850
-Guys. you remember Bonnie?
-Hi.

450
00:23:13.892 --> 00:23:15.685
And this is Jessie.

451
00:23:15.727 --> 00:23:18.397
[as Jessie] I ain't afraid
of nothin'. partner.

452
00:23:19.773 --> 00:23:22.651
Oh. You still play with toys?

453
00:23:22.692 --> 00:23:25.112
[friends laughing]

454
00:23:25.153 --> 00:23:26.279
[Bonnie gasps]

455
00:23:26.780 --> 00:23:28.907
Um... Uh...

456
00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:32.202
Uh. um... uh...

457
00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.578
No. Be right back.

458
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:36.331
-Here you go. sweetie.
-Dad. take these.

459
00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:37.749
But I thought
you wanted your toys?

460
00:23:37.791 --> 00:23:38.959
Dad. just go.

461
00:23:42.003 --> 00:23:43.547
[♪ ominous music plays]

462
00:23:43.588 --> 00:23:44.631
[gasps]

463
00:23:47.134 --> 00:23:48.218
Guys.

464
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:49.928
-I got my Lilypad.
-Bye!

465
00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:51.680
-[gasps]
-[Bonnie groans]

466
00:23:53.223 --> 00:23:54.307
No.

467
00:23:55.434 --> 00:23:56.726
[Bonnie grunts]

468
00:24:03.358 --> 00:24:04.526
[grunts]

469
00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:07.112
[panting]

470
00:24:09.531 --> 00:24:10.740
[groans]

471
00:24:11.908 --> 00:24:13.034
[grunts]

472
00:24:18.331 --> 00:24:19.541
[gasps]

473
00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:20.417
No. no. no.

474
00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:24.129
No. no. no. this is all wrong.

475
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:25.714
How is she
supposed to make friends

476
00:24:25.755 --> 00:24:27.299
if they ain't even
looking at each oth--

477
00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:28.425
[screams]

478
00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:30.635
Oh.

479
00:24:30.677 --> 00:24:32.471
-[gasps]
-[footsteps approaching]

480
00:24:34.973 --> 00:24:38.185
Oh. no.
Somebody lost their toys.

481
00:24:38.226 --> 00:24:39.352
What's that?

482
00:24:39.394 --> 00:24:41.855
I said
somebody lost their toys.

483
00:24:44.024 --> 00:24:45.275
Let's see.

484
00:24:45.317 --> 00:24:46.443
[gasps]

485
00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:49.404
They belong to an Emily.

486
00:24:49.446 --> 00:24:51.698
[driver]
Oh. and there's an address.

487
00:24:51.740 --> 00:24:53.909
-That's not too far from here.
-[gasps]

488
00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:55.535
We can drop them off.

489
00:25:04.085 --> 00:25:06.421
[phone]
Turn right onto Ranch Road.

490
00:25:13.428 --> 00:25:15.180
[phone] You've reached
your destination.

491
00:25:15.222 --> 00:25:16.681
[grunting]

492
00:25:16.723 --> 00:25:18.475
I'll just leave them here
in the mailbox.

493
00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:19.726
What's that?

494
00:25:19.768 --> 00:25:21.019
I'm leaving them
in the mailbox.

495
00:25:21.061 --> 00:25:22.562
-You're leaving me?
-Yes.

496
00:25:22.604 --> 00:25:24.439
[panting]
No. no. no.

497
00:25:24.481 --> 00:25:25.941
No. no. no.

498
00:25:27.567 --> 00:25:29.778
No! [panting]

499
00:25:29.819 --> 00:25:31.655
We cannot be here.

500
00:25:31.696 --> 00:25:35.200
We've gotta
get back to Bonnie!

501
00:25:35.242 --> 00:25:36.576
Come on. Bullseye. [grunts]

502
00:25:36.618 --> 00:25:38.662
[♪ adventurous music playing]

503
00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:40.622
[Jessie panting]

504
00:25:41.873 --> 00:25:43.083
[exclaims. grunts]

505
00:25:45.794 --> 00:25:47.837
[♪ ominous music playing]

506
00:25:50.882 --> 00:25:53.009
-[gasps]
-[grunts]

507
00:25:54.886 --> 00:25:56.179
[thuds]

508
00:25:56.930 --> 00:25:58.765
-[snorts]
-[Jessie shouts]

509
00:25:58.807 --> 00:25:59.766
[screams]

510
00:26:00.267 --> 00:26:01.935
Uh-oh! Uh! Oh!

511
00:26:01.977 --> 00:26:04.604
[chuckling] Whoa!

512
00:26:04.646 --> 00:26:05.981
Whoo!

513
00:26:06.022 --> 00:26:08.149
[laughing]

514
00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:10.652
Hi!

515
00:26:10.694 --> 00:26:13.697
Bullseye! You thinking
what I'm thinking?

516
00:26:13.738 --> 00:26:16.032
Yeah!
Yeah. I'm gonna speak critter.

517
00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:18.118
and we'll
ride this horse home!

518
00:26:18.159 --> 00:26:19.953
We're coming. Bonnie!

519
00:26:19.995 --> 00:26:22.497
Yeehaw!

520
00:26:22.539 --> 00:26:24.499
-[whinnies]
-[Jessie shouts]

521
00:26:24.541 --> 00:26:27.335
Whoa. whoa. whoa!
Wrong way. horsey!

522
00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:29.212
Wrong way!

523
00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:32.549
-[whinnies]
-Whoa. horsey! Whoa!

524
00:26:33.842 --> 00:26:36.511
No! No. no. no. no!

525
00:26:36.553 --> 00:26:39.264
-Whoa!
-[thudding]

526
00:26:42.934 --> 00:26:45.270
[Jessie coughing]

527
00:26:46.146 --> 00:26:47.564
[groans]

528
00:26:47.606 --> 00:26:49.858
[coughs. groans]

529
00:26:49.899 --> 00:26:50.984
[sighs]

530
00:26:51.568 --> 00:26:52.694
Bullseye?

531
00:26:52.736 --> 00:26:54.529
[horse whinnies. snorts]

532
00:26:55.447 --> 00:26:56.865
[Jessie] Oh!

533
00:26:56.906 --> 00:26:58.325
Thank goodness.
Come here. Help me.

534
00:26:59.409 --> 00:27:00.535
[person] Daffodil?

535
00:27:02.871 --> 00:27:04.247
Geez. are you all right?

536
00:27:04.289 --> 00:27:06.750
-[gasps]
-Did something spook you?

537
00:27:06.791 --> 00:27:08.668
Come on. girl. [clicks tongue]

538
00:27:08.710 --> 00:27:11.129
Come on. Good girl.

539
00:27:13.715 --> 00:27:14.674
Hmm?

540
00:27:15.175 --> 00:27:16.176
[gasps]

541
00:27:17.052 --> 00:27:18.553
Where'd you come from?

542
00:27:19.638 --> 00:27:21.348
[chuckling] He's perfect.

543
00:27:22.724 --> 00:27:25.435
No. Bullseye.

544
00:27:30.065 --> 00:27:32.567
Mmm... Hmm.

545
00:27:32.609 --> 00:27:34.569
Hmm.

546
00:27:34.611 --> 00:27:36.404
And how exactly will this help
us get Bonnie's attention?

547
00:27:36.446 --> 00:27:38.782
Well. when they come back
from the sleepover...

548
00:27:38.823 --> 00:27:40.575
-Careful. That tickles.
-...she'll enter the room.

549
00:27:40.617 --> 00:27:43.870
see Forky and Karen Beverly.
and remember the wedding.

550
00:27:43.912 --> 00:27:45.997
We are talking about
Bonnie. right?

551
00:27:46.039 --> 00:27:47.332
And not Jessie?

552
00:27:47.374 --> 00:27:48.792
Huh? [chuckles]

553
00:27:48.833 --> 00:27:51.252
Of course Bonnie.
[chuckles] Just Bonnie.

554
00:27:51.294 --> 00:27:52.837
Hey. what's everyone
talking about?

555
00:27:52.879 --> 00:27:54.756
Buzz is gonna
propose to Jessie.

556
00:27:54.798 --> 00:27:56.508
-Propose?
-[Trixie] Finally.

557
00:27:56.549 --> 00:27:57.884
Wait a minute. Wait...
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

558
00:27:57.926 --> 00:27:59.511
[stammers] I didn't say that.

559
00:27:59.552 --> 00:28:00.929
-You didn't not say it either.
-Well. I...

560
00:28:00.970 --> 00:28:02.639
Who. Buzz?

561
00:28:02.681 --> 00:28:04.307
Question. Is Woody gonna
perform the wedding ceremony?

562
00:28:04.349 --> 00:28:07.143
I haven't thought
that far in advance. Forky.

563
00:28:07.185 --> 00:28:08.937
Okay. Then why is Woody
at the window?

564
00:28:08.978 --> 00:28:10.730
[all gasp] Woody!

565
00:28:11.606 --> 00:28:12.607
Woody!

566
00:28:12.649 --> 00:28:14.234
-Hey. everybody!
-[all] Bo!

567
00:28:14.275 --> 00:28:16.027
Howdy. folks. Coast clear?

568
00:28:16.069 --> 00:28:17.445
The stage is yours. my friend.

569
00:28:17.487 --> 00:28:18.738
[all] Woody!

570
00:28:18.822 --> 00:28:20.824
-It's good to s...
-Wow.

571
00:28:20.865 --> 00:28:22.826
[♪ Western guitar plays]

572
00:28:22.867 --> 00:28:24.619
Pretty cowboy.

573
00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.162
Why are you wearing
a dress. Woody?

574
00:28:26.204 --> 00:28:28.415
It's called a poncho. Forky.

575
00:28:28.456 --> 00:28:29.999
Thought I'd change it up.

576
00:28:30.041 --> 00:28:31.042
Yeah?

577
00:28:33.378 --> 00:28:34.546
Well. Bo likes it.

578
00:28:35.338 --> 00:28:37.674
[sighs] It's good to be back.

579
00:28:38.341 --> 00:28:39.718
-Shiny.
-What?

580
00:28:39.759 --> 00:28:41.344
-[all] Nothing.
-Love the poncho.

581
00:28:41.386 --> 00:28:43.012
Someone needs a brown marker.

582
00:28:43.054 --> 00:28:45.056
Wow. Look what Bonnie's done
with the place.

583
00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:48.017
[chuckling] It's...
She really let things go.

584
00:28:48.101 --> 00:28:49.018
-Oh. my.
-Oh.

585
00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.979
I see Sammy got bigger.

586
00:28:51.020 --> 00:28:54.566
-Uh. that's Sammy number two.
-No.

587
00:28:54.607 --> 00:28:56.067
-[all] Yeah.
-I'll explain it.

588
00:28:56.109 --> 00:28:58.695
There was a Sammy number one.
and then he died.

589
00:28:58.737 --> 00:29:00.113
-Poor Samuel.
-[beeping]

590
00:29:00.155 --> 00:29:02.157
-Halt. Who goes there?
-Whoa. whoa. whoa.

591
00:29:02.198 --> 00:29:04.993
Sor... Sorry.
My name is Woody.

592
00:29:05.118 --> 00:29:07.370
I come in peace.
Used to live here.

593
00:29:07.412 --> 00:29:08.455
All right.

594
00:29:08.496 --> 00:29:09.664
[chuckles]

595
00:29:09.706 --> 00:29:11.166
It's been too long. cowboy.

596
00:29:12.041 --> 00:29:13.918
-How've you been?
-Ah. busy.

597
00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:16.629
Came here as fast as I could
after Jessie called for help.

598
00:29:16.671 --> 00:29:19.007
-Good thing we were in town.
-She called you?

599
00:29:19.048 --> 00:29:20.925
-Yeah. I'm her deputy.
-But I'm her deputy.

600
00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:23.261
-Uh...
-[chuckles]

601
00:29:23.303 --> 00:29:25.054
-That's odd.
-[chuckling] Well. well...

602
00:29:25.096 --> 00:29:26.681
there must be
a little mix-up here.

603
00:29:26.723 --> 00:29:28.641
-Well. no offense. Woody.
-Oh. none taken. None taken.

604
00:29:28.683 --> 00:29:29.851
But she literally

605
00:29:29.893 --> 00:29:31.561
-deputized me.
-Oh. is that so?

606
00:29:31.603 --> 00:29:33.188
-Woody. look. Eyes here.
-Uh-huh.

607
00:29:33.229 --> 00:29:35.356
-Star. Deputy. Me.
-Uh-huh.

608
00:29:35.398 --> 00:29:37.400
-No star.
-[stammers] I got you.

609
00:29:37.442 --> 00:29:38.902
Star. No star.

610
00:29:38.985 --> 00:29:41.237
-Oh. hey. Buzz. what is that?
-What? Where?

611
00:29:41.821 --> 00:29:42.781
Ow.

612
00:29:42.822 --> 00:29:43.948
-Hey. Wait...
-What?

613
00:29:43.990 --> 00:29:45.784
Just happy to help. Deputy.

614
00:29:45.825 --> 00:29:49.287
[sighs] Call me when
you're done helping. dear.

615
00:29:49.329 --> 00:29:50.497
[Woody] Thanks. Bo.

616
00:29:50.538 --> 00:29:51.831
[Duke] Okay. ladies.

617
00:29:51.873 --> 00:29:53.583
-[Bo] Girls weekend!
-Yes.

618
00:29:53.625 --> 00:29:55.502
Un. deux. trois!

619
00:29:55.543 --> 00:29:56.377
[horn beeps]

620
00:29:57.670 --> 00:29:59.047
Where is Jessie. anyway?

621
00:29:59.088 --> 00:30:00.840
Sleepover reconnaissance.

622
00:30:00.882 --> 00:30:02.550
Yeah. she and Bullseye are
helping Bonnie make friends.

623
00:30:02.592 --> 00:30:05.261
While fending off
the nefarious Lilypad.

624
00:30:05.303 --> 00:30:07.722
It's Dolly. by the way.
Glasses.

625
00:30:07.764 --> 00:30:09.182
Didn't you always
have glasses?

626
00:30:09.224 --> 00:30:10.475
What? No.

627
00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:12.685
We've got it handled. cowboy.

628
00:30:12.727 --> 00:30:14.312
As her deputy. I'm certain

629
00:30:14.354 --> 00:30:16.606
Jessie's resting
on a comfy pillow right now

630
00:30:16.648 --> 00:30:18.817
making all the difference
for Bonnie.

631
00:30:18.858 --> 00:30:21.110
[Jessie groaning. straining]

632
00:30:24.405 --> 00:30:25.990
[groaning continues]

633
00:30:26.032 --> 00:30:26.866
[sighs]

634
00:30:26.908 --> 00:30:27.867
[whinnies]

635
00:30:28.660 --> 00:30:30.578
[scoffs] You're no help.

636
00:30:30.620 --> 00:30:32.038
[gasps]

637
00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:33.498
Hey. you can help
get me out of here.

638
00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:35.041
[summons Daffodil]

639
00:30:35.083 --> 00:30:37.043
Come here. Come on.
Come on. Daffodil.

640
00:30:37.085 --> 00:30:38.586
Yeah. yeah. come over here.

641
00:30:38.628 --> 00:30:39.754
Come on. Come on.

642
00:30:39.796 --> 00:30:40.922
[gasps]

643
00:30:40.964 --> 00:30:42.757
-[snorts]
-[chuckles]

644
00:30:42.799 --> 00:30:44.843
Nice pig. Nice pig.

645
00:30:44.884 --> 00:30:46.553
Stinky pig.

646
00:30:46.594 --> 00:30:48.471
-[screams]
-[grunts]

647
00:30:48.513 --> 00:30:50.014
Hey. hey. there.

648
00:30:50.098 --> 00:30:51.683
[stammers]
I guess you'll have to do.

649
00:30:52.308 --> 00:30:54.644
Jimmy Dean?

650
00:30:54.686 --> 00:30:56.771
You mean. like. the... Oh. no.

651
00:30:56.896 --> 00:30:58.439
-[squeals]
-Oh!

652
00:30:58.481 --> 00:30:59.732
-Okay. Wow. that's your name?
-[grunting]

653
00:30:59.774 --> 00:31:00.900
Jimmy Dean?

654
00:31:00.942 --> 00:31:03.403
Take me to the house.

655
00:31:03.444 --> 00:31:04.863
-[squealing]
-[gasps]

656
00:31:04.904 --> 00:31:07.282
Golly gee whillikers!
It's working.

657
00:31:07.323 --> 00:31:08.908
[exclaiming]

658
00:31:08.950 --> 00:31:10.535
Hey! Ugh! Yuck!

659
00:31:10.577 --> 00:31:13.037
[gasping]
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa!

660
00:31:13.538 --> 00:31:14.914
Yes!

661
00:31:14.956 --> 00:31:18.293
Yes. Yes. good pig.
Good pig. Good--

662
00:31:18.334 --> 00:31:20.253
No. No. no. no.

663
00:31:20.295 --> 00:31:22.255
Bad pig. Oh. wrong way. Jimmy.

664
00:31:22.297 --> 00:31:25.049
Oh. no. no.
Wrong house. Jimmy.

665
00:31:25.091 --> 00:31:26.342
Wrong house. Wrong-- [grunts]

666
00:31:27.010 --> 00:31:28.636
[Jimmy grunting]

667
00:31:28.678 --> 00:31:29.804
No. [grunts]

668
00:31:29.846 --> 00:31:32.390
[panting. strains]

669
00:31:32.432 --> 00:31:33.850
-[Combat Carl] Blaze?
-[gasps]

670
00:31:34.392 --> 00:31:35.476
[all groan]

671
00:31:35.518 --> 00:31:36.936
False alarm. everyone.

672
00:31:37.312 --> 00:31:38.897
Um...

673
00:31:38.938 --> 00:31:41.441
Oh. apologies. Where are
Combat Carl's manners?

674
00:31:41.482 --> 00:31:43.359
[stammers] Welcome.
Please. take a seat.

675
00:31:43.401 --> 00:31:44.611
Oh. [chuckles]

676
00:31:44.652 --> 00:31:46.863
No. I've gotta get home.

677
00:31:46.905 --> 00:31:48.197
-No. no! Sit.
-Please. sit.

678
00:31:48.239 --> 00:31:49.866
-[speaks Spanish]
-Combat Carl insists.

679
00:31:49.908 --> 00:31:51.659
Oh. Okay.

680
00:31:51.701 --> 00:31:53.202
-[all clamoring]
-No. no. no!

681
00:31:53.328 --> 00:31:56.039
-Oh. sorry. I'm sorry.
-Any chair but that one.

682
00:31:56.080 --> 00:31:57.373
Who... Who sits there?

683
00:31:57.415 --> 00:31:58.791
[all] Blaze.

684
00:31:58.833 --> 00:32:01.502
Blaze. You mean the girl I saw
in the barn?

685
00:32:01.544 --> 00:32:02.629
She's your kid?

686
00:32:02.670 --> 00:32:04.756
[sighs] Isn't she swell?

687
00:32:04.797 --> 00:32:06.257
She loves her tea parties.

688
00:32:06.299 --> 00:32:08.843
And telling us
all her secrets.

689
00:32:08.885 --> 00:32:10.887
That's right.
Pizza With Sunglasses.

690
00:32:10.929 --> 00:32:12.096
To Blaze's return.

691
00:32:12.138 --> 00:32:13.973
[all] To Blaze's return!

692
00:32:14.015 --> 00:32:15.975
[sipping]

693
00:32:16.643 --> 00:32:17.977
Mmm. Rico.

694
00:32:18.436 --> 00:32:19.604
Ooh. hot.

695
00:32:19.687 --> 00:32:21.397
[smacks lips] Uh...

696
00:32:21.439 --> 00:32:26.152
How long has it been
since your Blaze last had tea?

697
00:32:27.946 --> 00:32:29.781
Things were
never really the same

698
00:32:29.822 --> 00:32:31.824
-once he arrived.
-He?

699
00:32:31.866 --> 00:32:34.702
Smarty Pants.
Blaze's first device.

700
00:32:34.744 --> 00:32:36.496
-You're sitting on him.
-What?

701
00:32:36.579 --> 00:32:38.831
[gasps] Holy butterscotch!

702
00:32:38.873 --> 00:32:39.749
[beeps]

703
00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:41.417
[♪ playing music]

704
00:32:41.459 --> 00:32:43.294
Why. hello there.
Pick a number.

705
00:32:43.336 --> 00:32:45.338
-Not again!
-Make it stop! Don't!

706
00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:47.465
-Oh. just kill me.
-Come on.

707
00:32:47.507 --> 00:32:49.008
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

708
00:32:49.050 --> 00:32:50.426
-Hey. hey!
-No! Don't!

709
00:32:50.468 --> 00:32:52.595
This...
This isn't the bathroom.

710
00:32:53.346 --> 00:32:54.514
How long have I been off?

711
00:32:54.555 --> 00:32:55.765
-Shut up. chair!
-We hate you.

712
00:32:55.807 --> 00:32:56.849
Turn him off.

713
00:32:56.891 --> 00:32:58.685
[groans] Gosh.

714
00:32:59.727 --> 00:33:03.147
Who's this little. old.
tiny grandma lady?

715
00:33:03.189 --> 00:33:06.067
-Gosh. what is wrong with him?
-Low batteries.

716
00:33:06.109 --> 00:33:07.443
[Smarty Pants groaning]

717
00:33:07.485 --> 00:33:09.070
Eggman?

718
00:33:09.112 --> 00:33:10.780
[groans] You're one of those
Pond devices.

719
00:33:10.822 --> 00:33:12.532
-[burps]
-[groans]

720
00:33:12.573 --> 00:33:14.200
I already have to put up with
a Lilypad back home.

721
00:33:14.242 --> 00:33:16.119
-Hey.
-I don't have time for this.

722
00:33:16.160 --> 00:33:19.580
[grunting] Your Blaze took my
horse into the house...

723
00:33:20.540 --> 00:33:23.001
and we gotta get back
to our own kid.

724
00:33:23.042 --> 00:33:25.586
Wait. wait. wait. wait.
You're going inside?

725
00:33:25.628 --> 00:33:28.631
-Take me with you. please!
-Not a chance.

726
00:33:28.673 --> 00:33:30.133
You need help pushing?

727
00:33:30.174 --> 00:33:32.301
I'm... [hiccups]
...great with pushing.

728
00:33:32.385 --> 00:33:34.554
You can do it. You can do it.
Like a choo-choo.

729
00:33:34.595 --> 00:33:36.097
- you can poop.
- No!

730
00:33:36.139 --> 00:33:37.849
How about you just wait here
with your friends?

731
00:33:37.890 --> 00:33:41.019
Spend another second with
Corporal No-Pants? [hiccups]

732
00:33:41.060 --> 00:33:42.729
I'm coming with you. cowgirl.

733
00:33:42.770 --> 00:33:44.814
No way. Your kind's caused me
enough trouble.

734
00:33:44.856 --> 00:33:46.274
My kind?

735
00:33:46.399 --> 00:33:47.900
-Take him!
-Please! Get him out of here!

736
00:33:47.942 --> 00:33:49.235
All he's good for is chair.

737
00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:52.530
I am not a chair!

738
00:33:52.572 --> 00:33:55.867
I am a potty trainer!

739
00:33:55.908 --> 00:33:58.536
Show some respect!

740
00:33:58.578 --> 00:34:01.873
Okay. listen. Raggedy Ann. All
these losers are outdoor toys.

741
00:34:01.914 --> 00:34:04.500
I'm the only one who's
done time inside. [hiccups]

742
00:34:04.542 --> 00:34:06.461
You wanna find your horsey?
Clippity-clop.

743
00:34:06.502 --> 00:34:09.047
I know exactly
where Blaze put him. okay?

744
00:34:09.088 --> 00:34:11.049
You need me.
You need me. You need me.

745
00:34:11.090 --> 00:34:13.051
You need me.
You need me. You need me.

746
00:34:14.719 --> 00:34:15.928
Hi.

747
00:34:16.679 --> 00:34:18.806
[Jessie] Move. Move.

748
00:34:19.348 --> 00:34:20.183
[all grunt]

749
00:34:22.435 --> 00:34:24.645
Hey. geez. Someone dim
the brightness out here.

750
00:34:24.687 --> 00:34:25.897
-Shut up.
-Would you try walking

751
00:34:25.938 --> 00:34:27.648
-a little less bouncy?
-Shut up.

752
00:34:27.690 --> 00:34:29.567
Quick. Lock the door before
they change their minds.

753
00:34:29.609 --> 00:34:30.568
Copy that.

754
00:34:32.653 --> 00:34:35.281
[♪ marching music playing]

755
00:34:44.832 --> 00:34:46.501
[gasps] Halt.

756
00:34:50.505 --> 00:34:52.507
[wailing sound playing]

757
00:34:56.677 --> 00:34:58.346
[sniffing]

758
00:35:00.431 --> 00:35:01.474
[wailing stops]

759
00:35:04.310 --> 00:35:05.478
-[sniffs]
-[chuckles]

760
00:35:06.646 --> 00:35:11.275
♪ Love is a song
That never ends ♪

761
00:35:11.317 --> 00:35:12.944
[Buzzes chuckle]

762
00:35:12.985 --> 00:35:15.238
♪ Life may be swift
And fleeting ♪

763
00:35:15.279 --> 00:35:18.366
[all chuckling]

764
00:35:18.407 --> 00:35:23.579
♪ Hope may die
Yet love's beautiful music ♪

765
00:35:23.621 --> 00:35:27.333
♪ Comes each day
Like the dawn-- ♪

766
00:35:27.375 --> 00:35:29.377
[♪ ominous music playing]

767
00:35:30.711 --> 00:35:32.839
Hon. I'm pretty sure
we go this way.

768
00:35:33.673 --> 00:35:34.841
[spouse] You sure?

769
00:35:34.882 --> 00:35:37.260
[grunting]

770
00:35:37.301 --> 00:35:38.719
[footsteps approaching]

771
00:35:38.761 --> 00:35:39.804
Save yourselves.

772
00:35:44.517 --> 00:35:46.894
It's this line here.

773
00:35:46.936 --> 00:35:48.980
If we follow it...

774
00:35:49.063 --> 00:35:50.815
-There's our camp.
-Oh. I see.

775
00:35:50.857 --> 00:35:52.150
Yeah. that looks right.

776
00:35:53.526 --> 00:35:55.403
Hey. wait for me. guys!

777
00:35:57.113 --> 00:35:59.699
-Whoa. No way.
-[all gasp]

778
00:35:59.740 --> 00:36:01.826
Hey. Morgan! Look at this.

779
00:36:01.868 --> 00:36:03.536
[Morgan]
Lucky. Hey. let me see it.

780
00:36:03.578 --> 00:36:04.620
Nope. Finders keepers.

781
00:36:04.745 --> 00:36:05.705
-Mom!
-Man down.

782
00:36:05.746 --> 00:36:07.415
-Code red.
-Code red.

783
00:36:07.456 --> 00:36:08.791
-Code red. Code red. Code red.
-Kids. be nice.

784
00:36:08.833 --> 00:36:11.711
Code red. Code red. Code red.

785
00:36:14.088 --> 00:36:16.966
Blaze. I'm going out.
Be back in an hour.

786
00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:18.217
[Blaze] Okay. Mom.

787
00:36:22.054 --> 00:36:24.182
[grunts. panting]

788
00:36:24.223 --> 00:36:26.184
Get Bullseye. get out.
Get Bullseye. get out.

789
00:36:26.225 --> 00:36:28.519
-Hey. cowgirl?
-Shh.

790
00:36:28.561 --> 00:36:30.813
-[gasps]
-Ooh. Forgot my keys.

791
00:36:32.982 --> 00:36:34.400
[Jessie gasps. exclaims]

792
00:36:34.442 --> 00:36:37.403
-Ugh! [coughing]
-[Smarty Pants groaning]

793
00:36:37.445 --> 00:36:38.946
Really don't feel so good.

794
00:36:39.071 --> 00:36:40.990
I think I'm gonna...
[burps] ...reboot.

795
00:36:41.032 --> 00:36:42.617
[♪ upbeat music playing]

796
00:36:42.658 --> 00:36:44.577
Shh. Quiet. quiet. quiet.
Quiet. quiet. quiet. quiet.

797
00:36:44.619 --> 00:36:46.454
-[grunts] Quiet.
-[♪ music stops]

798
00:36:48.372 --> 00:36:49.165
[gasps]

799
00:36:51.792 --> 00:36:53.836
[Smarty Pants] Wait. Wait.

800
00:36:53.878 --> 00:36:55.838
Wait. I'm back.

801
00:36:55.880 --> 00:36:58.090
I'm back home.

802
00:36:58.132 --> 00:37:02.136
-This is where it all started.
-[groans]

803
00:37:02.178 --> 00:37:03.304
Yeah.

804
00:37:03.346 --> 00:37:05.431
-It's all changed.
-[groans]

805
00:37:05.473 --> 00:37:07.516
[gasps] Smarty. no.

806
00:37:07.558 --> 00:37:09.977
I-I have to find Bullseye.
Wake up!

807
00:37:10.019 --> 00:37:12.813
-Need more juice.
-[beeping]

808
00:37:12.855 --> 00:37:14.774
Okay!
W-Where are the batteries?

809
00:37:14.815 --> 00:37:16.442
Where do I find the batteries?

810
00:37:16.484 --> 00:37:20.947
Bottom drawer.
next to the stamps.

811
00:37:22.615 --> 00:37:23.783
[strains]

812
00:37:29.288 --> 00:37:30.998
Why. hello there!
Pick a number.

813
00:37:31.040 --> 00:37:32.166
Is it number one?

814
00:37:32.208 --> 00:37:34.377
-Whoa! I feel great!
-Shh!

815
00:37:34.418 --> 00:37:36.045
-Look at me!
-Shh! No!

816
00:37:36.087 --> 00:37:37.797
-Yes! [laughs]
-No. we're not doing this now.

817
00:37:37.838 --> 00:37:38.881
-Not now.
-I am back!

818
00:37:38.923 --> 00:37:41.092
-Cut it out!
-[gasps]

819
00:37:41.133 --> 00:37:43.886
Snappy. Atlas.
They're still here!

820
00:37:43.970 --> 00:37:45.930
Oh! Bossy cowgirl.
we have to turn 'em back on.

821
00:37:45.972 --> 00:37:47.515
No! No way.

822
00:37:47.556 --> 00:37:49.475
The last thing this world
needs is more devices.

823
00:37:49.517 --> 00:37:51.269
What. what. what?

824
00:37:51.310 --> 00:37:53.104
You're just gonna shove 'em
back in the dark forever?

825
00:37:53.145 --> 00:37:55.147
Do you have any idea
what that's like?

826
00:37:55.189 --> 00:37:56.315
[♪ pensive music playing]

827
00:37:56.357 --> 00:37:57.566
[sighs]

828
00:37:57.608 --> 00:38:00.319
Fine.
We gotta make this quick.

829
00:38:00.361 --> 00:38:01.904
[laughs] Yes!

830
00:38:01.946 --> 00:38:04.073
Number one! You made number--

831
00:38:08.327 --> 00:38:09.954
-Atlas! Snappy!
-Smarty!

832
00:38:09.996 --> 00:38:11.872
-Smarty? Is that you?
-Is it really you?

833
00:38:11.914 --> 00:38:14.125
-It's really me! Yes!
-My goodness. You look great.

834
00:38:14.166 --> 00:38:15.876
-The AA-Team is back!
-Oh. my gosh. Yes!

835
00:38:15.918 --> 00:38:17.878
Mom brought us inside
after that tantrum Blaze had.

836
00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:19.463
and we never saw you again.

837
00:38:19.505 --> 00:38:21.090
-So tell me. What did I miss?
-Oh. my gosh.

838
00:38:21.132 --> 00:38:23.217
Well. we've been down
a long time too.

839
00:38:23.259 --> 00:38:26.053
But look! I could show you how
first and second grade went!

840
00:38:26.095 --> 00:38:27.471
Yeah. yeah. yeah.
Please do that. Yeah.

841
00:38:27.513 --> 00:38:29.682
Look at her!
She's so much older.

842
00:38:29.724 --> 00:38:31.267
-I know. right?
-She's adorable.

843
00:38:31.309 --> 00:38:33.060
-Isn't she?
-She got bangs that year.

844
00:38:33.102 --> 00:38:35.396
-Wait a minute. Where is that?
-That's Disneyland.

845
00:38:35.438 --> 00:38:36.605
Zoom in.
That's me in her pocket.

846
00:38:36.647 --> 00:38:38.524
Oh. flush.
You both went there?

847
00:38:38.566 --> 00:38:39.483
-[Snappy] Mm-hmm. For reals.
-[Atlas] It's so beautiful.

848
00:38:40.401 --> 00:38:42.278
And. uh.
that's the last of it.

849
00:38:42.320 --> 00:38:44.530
Next. it was just
a spinning rainbow wheel.

850
00:38:44.572 --> 00:38:46.073
Then... darkness.

851
00:38:46.115 --> 00:38:47.992
My entire SD card
flashed before my eyes.

852
00:38:48.034 --> 00:38:49.785
-[Smarty Pants] Wow.
-[Atlas] Aw.

853
00:38:49.827 --> 00:38:52.747
Okay. okay. I am glad you're
all powered up and stuff.

854
00:38:52.788 --> 00:38:54.749
but we're wasting time
I don't got.

855
00:38:54.790 --> 00:38:57.126
Oh. we're so grateful to you.
cowboy lady.

856
00:38:57.168 --> 00:38:59.045
Guys. guys. guys.
this is pushy cowgirl Jessie.

857
00:38:59.086 --> 00:39:01.213
She claims she's a sheriff.
Just go with it.

858
00:39:01.255 --> 00:39:03.341
-Blaze has her horse. Banzai--
-Bullseye!

859
00:39:03.382 --> 00:39:05.843
And I gotta get us back
to our kid. Bonnie. now.

860
00:39:05.885 --> 00:39:08.095
She needs us.
So. where is he. Smarty?

861
00:39:08.137 --> 00:39:10.848
All right. okay. I said
I'd tell ya. so I'll tell ya.

862
00:39:10.890 --> 00:39:12.850
-Drumroll please.
-[thudding]

863
00:39:12.892 --> 00:39:15.811
He's probably in the bedroom.

864
00:39:15.853 --> 00:39:18.564
Probably in the bedroom?
I could've guessed that.

865
00:39:18.606 --> 00:39:20.858
-And yet. you did not. Dusty.
-Dusty?

866
00:39:20.900 --> 00:39:23.194
Yeah. you know. like ancient.
elderly. mummified old fart.

867
00:39:23.235 --> 00:39:25.529
Or as I like to call it.
number 1.5.

868
00:39:25.571 --> 00:39:26.739
-I missed you. Smarty.
-[chuckles]

869
00:39:26.781 --> 00:39:28.407
You know what?

870
00:39:28.449 --> 00:39:30.242
-I've had enough of your cr--
-Oh. wait!

871
00:39:30.284 --> 00:39:32.203
I just had an idea that could
maybe help you get to Bonnie.

872
00:39:32.244 --> 00:39:34.538
-[sighs] What?
-It's a little technical.

873
00:39:34.580 --> 00:39:36.123
but if the three
of us link up--

874
00:39:36.165 --> 00:39:38.959
No. no. I am done
with this techno mumbo jumbo.

875
00:39:39.001 --> 00:39:42.296
No offense. but I'll be fine
getting back on my own.

876
00:39:42.338 --> 00:39:43.631
Offense taken!

877
00:39:48.469 --> 00:39:50.638
You're muted. Dave.
You're muted.

878
00:39:50.679 --> 00:39:52.515
Okay. There you go.

879
00:39:52.556 --> 00:39:54.100
[Dave] Only have a bit
of time left. One more time--

880
00:39:54.141 --> 00:39:55.351
[Blaze's dad]
You're muted again. Dave.

881
00:39:55.393 --> 00:39:57.520
[Smarty Pants grunting]

882
00:39:57.561 --> 00:39:59.021
Oh. cheese and crackers!

883
00:39:59.063 --> 00:40:00.815
What are you doing? Get back.

884
00:40:00.940 --> 00:40:02.900
You're not the only one
who misses their kid. okay?

885
00:40:02.942 --> 00:40:04.276
-Now help us up.
-[sighs]

886
00:40:04.318 --> 00:40:05.861
[all grunting]

887
00:40:05.903 --> 00:40:07.154
Careful. careful!
You're gonna unplug me.

888
00:40:07.196 --> 00:40:09.615
-[door opens]
-Blaze. I'm home.

889
00:40:09.657 --> 00:40:10.616
[Blaze] Hey. Mom!

890
00:40:10.658 --> 00:40:11.909
Back. back. back!

891
00:40:12.743 --> 00:40:14.703
-[toys grunting]
-Hey. Mom?

892
00:40:14.745 --> 00:40:17.164
-Wait a second. Is that...
-Is that big girl Blaze?

893
00:40:17.206 --> 00:40:19.542
-She's changed so much!
-Like overnight.

894
00:40:19.583 --> 00:40:21.419
-Is she here yet?
-[Blaze's mom] Not yet.

895
00:40:21.460 --> 00:40:22.628
Why don't you
try messaging her?

896
00:40:22.670 --> 00:40:24.004
-[Snappy] Whoa.
-She big. big.

897
00:40:24.046 --> 00:40:25.840
-She...
-[toilet flushes]

898
00:40:25.881 --> 00:40:28.050
She did it without me.

899
00:40:36.767 --> 00:40:38.144
-[Snappy] Wow.
-[gasps]

900
00:40:38.185 --> 00:40:39.562
-It's so pretty.
-It's so clean!

901
00:40:39.603 --> 00:40:40.813
[Smarty Pants]
When did she become neat?

902
00:40:40.855 --> 00:40:42.189
[Atlas] I can see the floor.

903
00:40:42.231 --> 00:40:43.774
[Snappy]
I can see me in the floor.

904
00:40:43.816 --> 00:40:45.693
It smells like vanilla.

905
00:40:45.734 --> 00:40:47.361
With hints of brown sugar.

906
00:40:47.403 --> 00:40:48.571
[Smarty Pants]
You know who I don't miss?

907
00:40:48.612 --> 00:40:50.448
[Snappy]
That stupid stuffed whale.

908
00:40:50.489 --> 00:40:51.615
-[Atlas] What was his name?
-[Smarty Pants] Spouty.

909
00:40:51.657 --> 00:40:52.950
[Snappy] The worst.

910
00:40:52.992 --> 00:40:54.201
[Smarty Pants]
Give me a break.

911
00:40:54.243 --> 00:40:55.494
[Snappy] Annoying.

912
00:40:55.536 --> 00:40:58.414
Seriously.
how much have we missed?

913
00:40:58.456 --> 00:41:00.082
Everything.

914
00:41:00.124 --> 00:41:02.585
Your Blaze ain't the kid
you remember anymore.

915
00:41:02.626 --> 00:41:03.961
How would you know?

916
00:41:04.003 --> 00:41:07.173
[sighs] I've seen
all this before.

917
00:41:07.214 --> 00:41:08.883
Spent a lot of years
under the bed

918
00:41:08.924 --> 00:41:11.719
watching my first kid
grow up without me.

919
00:41:13.804 --> 00:41:15.347
-Hey. that's our address.
-[GPS beeping]

920
00:41:15.389 --> 00:41:17.558
How old is Blaze anyway?
Nine. ten?

921
00:41:17.600 --> 00:41:19.185
Her room
looks like a teenager's.

922
00:41:19.226 --> 00:41:21.061
She's nine and a half.
thank you very much.

923
00:41:21.103 --> 00:41:23.856
It's 'cause you devices
make 'em change so fast.

924
00:41:23.898 --> 00:41:25.524
[groans] I gotta get back.

925
00:41:25.566 --> 00:41:27.443
-So. where--
-[whinnies]

926
00:41:28.152 --> 00:41:30.488
Bullseye! Thank goodness.

927
00:41:31.530 --> 00:41:33.991
Uh-huh.
they seem nice. Bullseye.

928
00:41:34.033 --> 00:41:35.284
but we have to go now.

929
00:41:35.326 --> 00:41:36.994
Wait. wait. wait. wait.

930
00:41:37.036 --> 00:41:39.288
So you're saying that
this was your room too?

931
00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:41.040
-Yes.
-[scoffs] Really?

932
00:41:41.081 --> 00:41:43.083
-[chuckling]
-What. you calling me a liar?

933
00:41:43.125 --> 00:41:44.168
No...

934
00:41:45.169 --> 00:41:46.795
Yeah. Yeah. liar.

935
00:41:46.837 --> 00:41:48.297
[sighs]

936
00:41:48.339 --> 00:41:49.840
[♪ tense music playing]

937
00:41:49.882 --> 00:41:51.509
There's a knot in the ceiling.

938
00:41:51.550 --> 00:41:53.302
looks like an angry eye
when you squint at it.

939
00:41:53.344 --> 00:41:54.929
Window's got a small crack

940
00:41:54.970 --> 00:41:56.639
like a spider in
the upper right-hand corner.

941
00:41:56.680 --> 00:41:58.974
And out on that
tire swing hill.

942
00:41:59.016 --> 00:42:01.644
Emily and I would play
every summer afternoon.

943
00:42:01.685 --> 00:42:03.395
Now. Bullseye. let's go.

944
00:42:03.437 --> 00:42:05.356
Uh. you're welcome.

945
00:42:05.397 --> 00:42:08.526
For what? You didn't help me
at all. You were--

946
00:42:08.567 --> 00:42:10.945
What? Go on. Say it.

947
00:42:13.239 --> 00:42:14.990
-Useless.
-[gasps]

948
00:42:15.032 --> 00:42:16.575
-Oh. no. she didn't.
-Oh. snap!

949
00:42:16.617 --> 00:42:18.494
-[Jimmy Dean snorting]
-[gasps]

950
00:42:18.536 --> 00:42:20.454
Oh. no. Not the pig!

951
00:42:22.414 --> 00:42:25.876
[♪ "I Love It" playing
through headphones]

952
00:42:25.918 --> 00:42:27.711
-[Blaze humming]
-[snorting]

953
00:42:27.753 --> 00:42:28.963
Jimmy got big.

954
00:42:30.256 --> 00:42:32.675
Lay it on me. Jimmy Dean!

955
00:42:32.716 --> 00:42:36.387
Who's coming? Sally's coming.
Who's coming? Sally's coming.

956
00:42:36.428 --> 00:42:40.099
Yeah. yeah. She's coming.
She's coming to my house.

957
00:42:41.141 --> 00:42:43.352
Hey. Mom!
Sally's texting me right now.

958
00:42:43.394 --> 00:42:44.770
She's probably on her way.

959
00:42:49.108 --> 00:42:51.151
[♪ melancholy music playing]

960
00:42:54.488 --> 00:42:55.739
[sighs]

961
00:43:02.788 --> 00:43:04.790
[sobbing]

962
00:43:08.544 --> 00:43:10.421
[snorting]

963
00:43:16.969 --> 00:43:20.639
You'll be my friend.
right. Jimmy?

964
00:43:25.561 --> 00:43:26.770
Always.

965
00:43:27.813 --> 00:43:32.651
By the way.
your hair looks so good today.

966
00:43:32.693 --> 00:43:34.028
[chuckles]

967
00:43:34.069 --> 00:43:35.321
Thank you. Jimmy.

968
00:43:38.574 --> 00:43:41.076
She's perfect!

969
00:43:41.118 --> 00:43:42.494
[blusters]

970
00:43:42.536 --> 00:43:44.538
We gotta get Blaze
to meet Bonnie.

971
00:43:44.580 --> 00:43:46.040
[chuckles]

972
00:43:46.081 --> 00:43:47.499
[snoring]

973
00:43:47.541 --> 00:43:48.584
-Bonnie.
-[gasps]

974
00:43:48.626 --> 00:43:49.710
Tag. you're it!

975
00:43:49.752 --> 00:43:50.919
We're home.

976
00:43:50.961 --> 00:43:52.963
Hi. hon.
How was the sleepover?

977
00:43:53.005 --> 00:43:54.256
I don't wanna talk about it.

978
00:43:54.298 --> 00:43:56.425
-Why? What happened?
-Nothing.

979
00:43:56.467 --> 00:43:57.676
That doesn't sound good.

980
00:43:57.718 --> 00:43:59.178
I don't see Jessie.

981
00:43:59.219 --> 00:44:00.304
Calm down. lover boy.

982
00:44:00.346 --> 00:44:01.513
Your fiancee's coming.

983
00:44:01.555 --> 00:44:02.890
Fiancee?

984
00:44:02.931 --> 00:44:05.225
Buzz Lightyear.
you never told me.

985
00:44:05.267 --> 00:44:08.437
I know. Isn't it exciting?
Well. it's not official yet.

986
00:44:08.479 --> 00:44:10.272
I have to. you know. ask her.

987
00:44:10.314 --> 00:44:12.232
Uh. FYI. I am ordained.

988
00:44:12.274 --> 00:44:14.109
-Since when?
-Last Halloween.

989
00:44:14.151 --> 00:44:15.819
Bonnie made me
a haunted priest. remember?

990
00:44:15.861 --> 00:44:17.154
-[toys] Oh. yeah.
-Guys. places.

991
00:44:17.196 --> 00:44:18.238
Bonnie's coming.

992
00:44:20.491 --> 00:44:21.909
[Bonnie's mom]
Did you make some friends?

993
00:44:21.950 --> 00:44:22.993
I guess so.

994
00:44:23.035 --> 00:44:24.578
Aw. she looks awful.

995
00:44:24.620 --> 00:44:25.829
Does anyone see Jessie?

996
00:44:26.914 --> 00:44:28.499
[Woody] So. that's Lilypad?

997
00:44:28.540 --> 00:44:30.209
[Bonnie's mom]
How about I make you a snack?

998
00:44:30.250 --> 00:44:32.586
[Bonnie]
Yes. please. I'm starving.

999
00:44:32.628 --> 00:44:35.464
Jessie. [grunts]
Jessie. Bullseye.

1000
00:44:35.506 --> 00:44:36.757
-Where are you?
-Oh. no. oh. no.

1001
00:44:36.799 --> 00:44:38.342
Is this not the right version?

1002
00:44:38.384 --> 00:44:40.260
What? Where's Jessie?
Where's Bullseye?

1003
00:44:40.302 --> 00:44:42.429
I'm a little busy
helping Bonnie right now.

1004
00:44:42.471 --> 00:44:44.306
What on earth happened
at that sleepover?

1005
00:44:44.348 --> 00:44:45.766
Excuse me. What are you?

1006
00:44:45.808 --> 00:44:47.017
Are you like
some sort of old man toy?

1007
00:44:47.059 --> 00:44:48.894
What?

1008
00:44:48.936 --> 00:44:50.270
She thinks you're old
because you're bald. Woody.

1009
00:44:50.312 --> 00:44:51.855
-Why. you little--
-Where's Jessie?

1010
00:44:51.897 --> 00:44:54.024
What happened to Bonnie?
She looks miserable.

1011
00:44:54.066 --> 00:44:55.776
Uh. the girls may have played
hide-and-seek

1012
00:44:55.818 --> 00:44:57.778
and. um.
forgotten to find Bonnie.

1013
00:44:57.820 --> 00:44:59.113
-[all gasp]
-Poor Bonnie.

1014
00:44:59.154 --> 00:45:00.364
How could you let that happen?

1015
00:45:00.406 --> 00:45:02.700
I didn't. You toys did this!

1016
00:45:02.741 --> 00:45:05.411
These girls have been
on The Pond for over a year.

1017
00:45:05.452 --> 00:45:07.204
but Bonnie is behind

1018
00:45:07.246 --> 00:45:09.164
because all of the time
she's been playing with you!

1019
00:45:09.206 --> 00:45:10.791
I need to bring her
up to speed fast.

1020
00:45:10.833 --> 00:45:12.668
starting with Turtle Tag.

1021
00:45:12.710 --> 00:45:14.211
It's the quickest way for her
to connect with the girls.

1022
00:45:14.253 --> 00:45:15.838
I'm only gonna ask
one more time. frog.

1023
00:45:15.879 --> 00:45:17.089
Where is Jessie?

1024
00:45:17.131 --> 00:45:18.507
Not my problem. I'm very busy.

1025
00:45:18.549 --> 00:45:20.217
-[all gasp]
-That's it.

1026
00:45:20.259 --> 00:45:21.343
-We'll make her talk.
-I'll do it. Woody.

1027
00:45:21.385 --> 00:45:22.761
-[grunts]
-Hey! Hey!

1028
00:45:22.803 --> 00:45:24.263
-I got it. I'll--
-I got it. Buzz. No.

1029
00:45:24.304 --> 00:45:25.556
-[Lilypad] Back off. buddy.
-I got this. Ow!

1030
00:45:25.597 --> 00:45:27.141
Do not touch me. Don't touch--

1031
00:45:27.182 --> 00:45:28.434
Where's Jessie?

1032
00:45:29.309 --> 00:45:31.895
Okay.
You toys are out of here.

1033
00:45:31.937 --> 00:45:33.313
[♪ ominous music playing]

1034
00:45:33.355 --> 00:45:34.606
[gasps] Wait.
She's doing something.

1035
00:45:35.941 --> 00:45:38.277
-So long. toys.
-[alarm blaring]

1036
00:45:38.318 --> 00:45:39.528
[shouts]

1037
00:45:39.570 --> 00:45:41.238
-Turn her off!
-Turn her off!

1038
00:45:41.280 --> 00:45:42.656
I can't! I can't!
It's not responding!

1039
00:45:42.698 --> 00:45:43.741
I have plastic fingers!

1040
00:45:43.782 --> 00:45:44.783
She's coming.

1041
00:45:45.576 --> 00:45:46.744
[alarm stops]

1042
00:45:51.457 --> 00:45:52.958
You sure you want me
to take these toys?

1043
00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:54.209
Mm-hmm.

1044
00:45:54.251 --> 00:45:56.086
Okay. It's your room.

1045
00:45:57.463 --> 00:45:58.547
[gasps]

1046
00:45:59.006 --> 00:46:00.758
No!

1047
00:46:00.799 --> 00:46:02.134
They'll be in the garage
if you want them.

1048
00:46:02.176 --> 00:46:03.218
Yep.

1049
00:46:06.346 --> 00:46:09.600
[Mr. Pricklepants] I now
pronounce us in storage.

1050
00:46:11.727 --> 00:46:14.104
[chuckles]
Playing with you is fun.

1051
00:46:16.857 --> 00:46:18.484
Okay. Now what do we d--

1052
00:46:19.276 --> 00:46:21.570
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1053
00:46:22.404 --> 00:46:23.655
[sighs]

1054
00:46:26.492 --> 00:46:29.119
Don't worry. Buzz.
We're gonna find her.

1055
00:46:29.870 --> 00:46:30.871
I promise.

1056
00:46:31.872 --> 00:46:34.166
[sighs]

1057
00:46:35.292 --> 00:46:38.712
Woody. I know it's just
a pretend ceremony.

1058
00:46:38.754 --> 00:46:41.006
and Bonnie usually
decides these things. but...

1059
00:46:42.216 --> 00:46:44.885
Well. if it were up to me.

1060
00:46:46.094 --> 00:46:47.304
you'd be my best man.

1061
00:46:47.346 --> 00:46:49.014
[gasps]

1062
00:46:49.056 --> 00:46:50.307
Buzz. I...

1063
00:46:51.016 --> 00:46:52.643
I'd be honored.

1064
00:46:52.684 --> 00:46:54.978
[sighs] But Jessie
will never speak to me again

1065
00:46:55.020 --> 00:46:57.689
now that I've let Lily
take charge of the room.

1066
00:46:57.731 --> 00:46:59.316
Wait a min-- Take charge.

1067
00:46:59.358 --> 00:47:01.151
-I tried to.
-No. no. no. Buzz. that's it.

1068
00:47:01.276 --> 00:47:02.361
What is?

1069
00:47:02.402 --> 00:47:04.238
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1070
00:47:11.954 --> 00:47:13.413
Tomorrow morning.

1071
00:47:13.455 --> 00:47:15.415
everyone will wake up
fully recharged...

1072
00:47:16.333 --> 00:47:19.044
except Lilypad.

1073
00:47:19.086 --> 00:47:22.506
And then we'll make Lily
tell us... Where's Jessie?

1074
00:47:27.302 --> 00:47:28.971
[Blaze snoring]

1075
00:47:29.012 --> 00:47:30.722
Oh. finally.

1076
00:47:35.853 --> 00:47:37.521
Psst. Hey.

1077
00:47:37.563 --> 00:47:38.897
[Smarty Pants]
It's okay. Just ignore her.

1078
00:47:38.939 --> 00:47:40.023
-[Atlas] Shh. shh.
-[Snappy] Quiet!

1079
00:47:40.065 --> 00:47:42.109
[Smarty Pants] Nobody's home.

1080
00:47:42.150 --> 00:47:44.486
-I can hear you.
-[Snappy] Smarty!

1081
00:47:44.528 --> 00:47:46.655
-What? I used a faraway voice.
-[Atlas] Come on. man!

1082
00:47:46.697 --> 00:47:48.574
-Look. Camera--
-It's Snappy.

1083
00:47:48.615 --> 00:47:50.033
Right. Snappy.

1084
00:47:50.075 --> 00:47:51.535
You said there was
a way you could help us

1085
00:47:51.577 --> 00:47:53.120
get to Bonnie. right?
So. what is it?

1086
00:47:53.161 --> 00:47:55.163
[Smarty Pants]
She did say that. didn't she?

1087
00:47:55.205 --> 00:47:56.915
That sounds. I don't know...

1088
00:47:56.957 --> 00:47:59.126
-[Snappy] Useful?
-That's it. yeah.

1089
00:47:59.167 --> 00:48:01.461
Too bad we're useless!

1090
00:48:01.503 --> 00:48:03.630
-[Snappy] Right!
-[Atlas] Yeah! Remember?

1091
00:48:04.506 --> 00:48:06.133
-[blusters]
-[sighs]

1092
00:48:06.174 --> 00:48:09.136
I'm sorry
I called you useless.

1093
00:48:09.177 --> 00:48:13.891
You three
are definitely of use...

1094
00:48:14.474 --> 00:48:15.350
somehow.

1095
00:48:16.560 --> 00:48:18.395
-[Snappy] Worst apology ever.
-[Atlas] Just awful.

1096
00:48:18.437 --> 00:48:20.564
[Smarty Pants] Now I want
an apology for that apology.

1097
00:48:20.606 --> 00:48:22.274
[sighs]

1098
00:48:22.316 --> 00:48:26.028
Please. I know I messed up.

1099
00:48:26.069 --> 00:48:29.281
I was wrong
about your kid. Blaze.

1100
00:48:29.323 --> 00:48:33.493
She's creative and silly

1101
00:48:33.577 --> 00:48:36.246
in a way
other kids don't really get.

1102
00:48:36.914 --> 00:48:38.332
[stammers] Am I right?

1103
00:48:47.215 --> 00:48:48.467
Go on.

1104
00:48:49.217 --> 00:48:51.637
Well. our kid's like that too.

1105
00:48:51.678 --> 00:48:54.056
And I think
they'd really like each other.

1106
00:48:54.097 --> 00:48:56.475
So. fine.
if you don't want to help me.

1107
00:48:56.516 --> 00:48:58.393
let's just help our kids.

1108
00:48:59.686 --> 00:49:01.271
All right. twist my handle.

1109
00:49:01.313 --> 00:49:02.814
Yeah! We're making friends.

1110
00:49:02.856 --> 00:49:04.149
-F-R-E-N-D.
-With an "I."

1111
00:49:04.191 --> 00:49:05.484
[Snappy] F-R-I-N-D.

1112
00:49:05.525 --> 00:49:07.486
Great! So.
how do we connect them?

1113
00:49:07.527 --> 00:49:10.405
You said your kid's device was
on The Pond like me. right?

1114
00:49:10.447 --> 00:49:14.451
Right! So Smarty. Atlas and I
are all compatible. see?

1115
00:49:14.493 --> 00:49:16.286
And I could take
a picture of you.

1116
00:49:16.328 --> 00:49:18.455
-Okay. act like a toy.
-O-Okay.

1117
00:49:20.290 --> 00:49:22.459
Uh. not very photogenic.
are they?

1118
00:49:22.501 --> 00:49:24.044
-And Atlas can add text to it.
-Mm-hmm.

1119
00:49:25.671 --> 00:49:27.631
-Then we post it on The Pond.
-[Atlas] Yep.

1120
00:49:27.673 --> 00:49:28.757
Where Bonnie is!

1121
00:49:28.799 --> 00:49:30.384
[all] Ta-da!

1122
00:49:30.425 --> 00:49:31.969
-Great! So. you sent it?
-[♪ gentle music playing]

1123
00:49:32.010 --> 00:49:33.512
No. Still going.

1124
00:49:33.553 --> 00:49:35.013
[sighs]

1125
00:49:37.099 --> 00:49:38.266
How about now?

1126
00:49:38.308 --> 00:49:40.727
[exclaims] Still going.

1127
00:49:40.769 --> 00:49:42.813
Still going?
How is that possible?

1128
00:49:42.854 --> 00:49:44.898
Look at my eyes! The little
toilet roll's still spinning.

1129
00:49:44.940 --> 00:49:46.566
I'm only as fast
as my operating system.

1130
00:49:46.692 --> 00:49:48.652
So just slow your roll.
all right?

1131
00:49:49.903 --> 00:49:51.488
-[chimes]
-There. It's sent.

1132
00:49:51.530 --> 00:49:54.074
Finally. Now what?

1133
00:49:54.116 --> 00:49:55.492
Now. we wait.

1134
00:49:55.534 --> 00:49:57.035
Yeah. everyone's still asleep.

1135
00:49:57.077 --> 00:49:58.578
We gotta wait for Bonnie
to wake up and see the post.

1136
00:49:58.662 --> 00:50:01.081
[groans. sighs]

1137
00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:05.877
Hey. I know!
We could play a game.

1138
00:50:05.919 --> 00:50:06.795
-Yes!
-Yeah!

1139
00:50:06.837 --> 00:50:07.838
-A game?
-Yeah!

1140
00:50:07.879 --> 00:50:09.089
It was Blaze's favorite.

1141
00:50:09.131 --> 00:50:10.757
It's called "Pick the Poop."

1142
00:50:10.799 --> 00:50:12.009
You try and hit the button

1143
00:50:12.050 --> 00:50:13.927
when the poop
shows up over it.

1144
00:50:13.969 --> 00:50:15.220
Hey. Smarty.

1145
00:50:16.054 --> 00:50:19.933
I will never play that game.

1146
00:50:19.975 --> 00:50:23.186
[chuckles] They all say that.

1147
00:50:24.438 --> 00:50:26.481
[insects chirping]

1148
00:50:26.523 --> 00:50:27.899
[child laughing]

1149
00:50:27.941 --> 00:50:29.317
[sibling] Come on!

1150
00:50:29.359 --> 00:50:30.861
-It's my turn.
-[mom] Okay. you two.

1151
00:50:30.902 --> 00:50:32.946
Time to stop playing
with your new toy.

1152
00:50:32.988 --> 00:50:34.906
-It's bedtime.
-[children groan]

1153
00:50:34.948 --> 00:50:36.992
-Already?
-Do we have to?

1154
00:50:37.034 --> 00:50:38.827
-[mom] Yeah. come on.
-[children groan]

1155
00:50:38.869 --> 00:50:40.871
[♪ tense music playing]

1156
00:51:12.444 --> 00:51:13.653
[laptop beeps]

1157
00:51:13.695 --> 00:51:14.905
Huh?

1158
00:51:24.122 --> 00:51:29.294
[mom] "And they had splendid
games together. in whispers.

1159
00:51:29.336 --> 00:51:32.214
when Nana had gone away
to her supper

1160
00:51:32.255 --> 00:51:34.007
and left
the night-light burning

1161
00:51:34.049 --> 00:51:36.176
on the mantelpiece.

1162
00:51:36.218 --> 00:51:39.429
And when the boy
dropped off to sleep.

1163
00:51:39.471 --> 00:51:43.809
the rabbit would
snuggle down close under

1164
00:51:43.850 --> 00:51:45.393
-his little. warm chin..."
-[beeping]

1165
00:51:45.435 --> 00:51:46.895
Sir.

1166
00:51:46.937 --> 00:51:50.065
"...and dream
with the boy's hands

1167
00:51:50.107 --> 00:51:53.652
clasped close
round him all night."

1168
00:51:59.908 --> 00:52:01.201
Hmm.

1169
00:52:02.369 --> 00:52:04.621
-[gasp] Star Command.
-Star Command.

1170
00:52:04.663 --> 00:52:06.081
-Star Command.
-Star Command.

1171
00:52:12.546 --> 00:52:14.756
[all] Star Command.

1172
00:52:16.466 --> 00:52:18.844
-[birds chirping]
-[groans]

1173
00:52:19.928 --> 00:52:23.014
[yawns. sighs]

1174
00:52:24.141 --> 00:52:25.433
What? No. no. no!

1175
00:52:25.475 --> 00:52:27.018
Dad! Dad!

1176
00:52:27.060 --> 00:52:28.770
What? What is it?

1177
00:52:28.812 --> 00:52:30.605
Lily's not working!
I'm missing Turtle Tag!

1178
00:52:30.647 --> 00:52:32.941
Kara. Chelsea and Heidi
play it every morning.

1179
00:52:32.983 --> 00:52:35.152
-I can't miss it. Dad!
-It's okay.

1180
00:52:35.193 --> 00:52:36.528
I plugged it back in.

1181
00:52:36.570 --> 00:52:38.196
We just need to wait
for it to charge.

1182
00:52:38.238 --> 00:52:39.865
But it's not okay!
I'm gonna miss the game!

1183
00:52:39.906 --> 00:52:41.950
Sweetie. there's nothing
we can do for now.

1184
00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:43.869
-[Bonnie groans]
-[door closes]

1185
00:52:43.910 --> 00:52:46.496
Aha! Success. huh?
Look at that.

1186
00:52:46.538 --> 00:52:47.831
That's phase one.

1187
00:52:47.873 --> 00:52:49.791
-And now. phase two.
-Phase two.

1188
00:52:49.833 --> 00:52:51.543
Well. I thought I was gonna
initiate phase two.

1189
00:52:51.585 --> 00:52:53.920
I initiate phase two.
We thumb wrestled over this.

1190
00:52:53.962 --> 00:52:55.505
All right. fine.

1191
00:52:55.547 --> 00:52:57.716
And then we'll have
a little talk

1192
00:52:57.757 --> 00:52:59.509
with our froggy friend.

1193
00:53:00.343 --> 00:53:03.305
-[toy beeping]
-[Blaze snoring]

1194
00:53:03.346 --> 00:53:05.182
[grunting]

1195
00:53:05.223 --> 00:53:07.976
-One. two. one. two. two...
-I hate this game.

1196
00:53:08.018 --> 00:53:09.728
-...one. two. one...
-Please make it stop.

1197
00:53:11.146 --> 00:53:12.939
-Mighty Wiper!
-[Atlas shushes]

1198
00:53:12.981 --> 00:53:15.025
-Again. again. again!
-I think you need a break.

1199
00:53:15.066 --> 00:53:16.985
I can't feel my buttons.

1200
00:53:17.027 --> 00:53:19.404
-Just one more time! Come on!
-That's enough play for now.

1201
00:53:19.446 --> 00:53:21.072
Play? [scoffs]

1202
00:53:21.114 --> 00:53:22.532
That's just a game.
That's not playing.

1203
00:53:22.574 --> 00:53:23.533
What's the difference?

1204
00:53:23.575 --> 00:53:25.076
You know. real play.

1205
00:53:26.745 --> 00:53:28.288
You're kidding. right?

1206
00:53:28.330 --> 00:53:30.207
You've never seen Blaze
play with a toy?

1207
00:53:31.541 --> 00:53:32.876
How long
were you guys with her?

1208
00:53:32.918 --> 00:53:33.960
-Three months.
-Ten months.

1209
00:53:34.002 --> 00:53:35.045
-Six months.
-Months?

1210
00:53:35.086 --> 00:53:36.755
What? Too long?

1211
00:53:36.796 --> 00:53:39.174
Too short! [groans]
Guys. you missed all the fun!

1212
00:53:39.216 --> 00:53:40.383
Hey. we're fun.

1213
00:53:40.425 --> 00:53:43.011
I mean fun. fun.
Make-believe fun.

1214
00:53:47.349 --> 00:53:48.725
Just look at her.

1215
00:53:51.353 --> 00:53:53.355
Oh. yeah. She plays.

1216
00:53:53.396 --> 00:53:55.565
Oh. yeah? Prove it.

1217
00:53:55.607 --> 00:53:59.069
Okay. Smarty Pants. We will.

1218
00:54:01.029 --> 00:54:03.907
[sniffs. snorting]

1219
00:54:03.949 --> 00:54:05.408
[groans]

1220
00:54:05.992 --> 00:54:07.369
Morning. Jimmy.

1221
00:54:08.495 --> 00:54:11.122
Ready for breakfast? Hmm?

1222
00:54:15.710 --> 00:54:17.170
Whoa.

1223
00:54:17.212 --> 00:54:19.923
Hey. Mom!
Where'd you find the cowgirl?

1224
00:54:19.965 --> 00:54:21.633
[chuckles]

1225
00:54:21.675 --> 00:54:23.218
I ain't afraid
of nothin'. partner.

1226
00:54:23.260 --> 00:54:26.388
-[chuckles]
- Yeehaw! Let's play!

1227
00:54:26.429 --> 00:54:27.472
[gasps]

1228
00:54:28.348 --> 00:54:29.641
Yeah.

1229
00:54:31.476 --> 00:54:32.811
[chuckles]

1230
00:54:32.852 --> 00:54:34.479
Wait a minute.

1231
00:54:36.898 --> 00:54:38.191
[Blaze chuckles] Hmm.

1232
00:54:38.233 --> 00:54:39.276
Neigh!

1233
00:54:39.317 --> 00:54:40.986
Well. flush me.

1234
00:54:41.027 --> 00:54:43.029
Blaze is actually gonna play.

1235
00:54:43.071 --> 00:54:45.782
[vocalizing] Here we go!

1236
00:54:45.824 --> 00:54:47.575
[♪ ballroom music playing]

1237
00:54:48.493 --> 00:54:49.786
-M'la-- [gasps]
-[gasps. chuckles]

1238
00:54:51.413 --> 00:54:53.665
M'lady Davenport.

1239
00:54:54.708 --> 00:54:57.335
I present Her Royal Highness.

1240
00:54:57.377 --> 00:54:59.504
Jimmy Queen.

1241
00:54:59.546 --> 00:55:01.131
[snorting]

1242
00:55:01.172 --> 00:55:04.301
[clears throat]
Your Highness. how kind of you

1243
00:55:04.342 --> 00:55:05.969
to invite me
to your royal ball--

1244
00:55:06.011 --> 00:55:08.471
[babbling]

1245
00:55:08.513 --> 00:55:10.765
Jimmy!
This is your big moment.

1246
00:55:10.807 --> 00:55:13.184
-[snorting]
-[toys beeping]

1247
00:55:14.436 --> 00:55:16.229
What you got there. Jimmy?

1248
00:55:16.271 --> 00:55:17.647
[snorting]

1249
00:55:17.689 --> 00:55:19.482
Whoa.

1250
00:55:20.650 --> 00:55:22.861
[chuckling] I can't believe
I still have these.

1251
00:55:23.653 --> 00:55:25.613
[gasps] Wait a minute.

1252
00:55:26.990 --> 00:55:30.035
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1253
00:55:30.076 --> 00:55:31.536
[Snappy] Agent Clydesdale.

1254
00:55:31.578 --> 00:55:33.079
your suitor
is approaching now.

1255
00:55:33.121 --> 00:55:34.414
[gasps]

1256
00:55:34.456 --> 00:55:37.334
So. we meet again.
Agent Sheet-land.

1257
00:55:37.375 --> 00:55:39.002
It's pronounced Shet-land.
"Shet."

1258
00:55:39.044 --> 00:55:40.420
That's what I said.

1259
00:55:40.462 --> 00:55:42.172
Well. Agent Clydesdale.
or should I say.

1260
00:55:42.213 --> 00:55:44.507
Lady Davenport.
have you spotted it yet?

1261
00:55:44.549 --> 00:55:45.800
You mean. the bomb?

1262
00:55:45.842 --> 00:55:47.218
Yes! Shh! Quiet!

1263
00:55:47.260 --> 00:55:48.762
Snappy.
do you have eyes on it?

1264
00:55:48.803 --> 00:55:50.638
Not yet. Atlas. do you copy?

1265
00:55:52.098 --> 00:55:54.309
Agents! The bomb
is right on top of you!

1266
00:55:54.351 --> 00:55:56.728
-[beeping]
-[gasps] Where? Where?

1267
00:55:56.770 --> 00:55:58.188
[laughs]

1268
00:55:58.229 --> 00:56:01.441
Where you never suspected.
Agent Clydesdale!

1269
00:56:01.483 --> 00:56:04.110
-[laughing]
-[guests gasping]

1270
00:56:04.819 --> 00:56:07.197
-[gasps]
-[laughs]

1271
00:56:07.238 --> 00:56:09.449
But where is the bomb?

1272
00:56:09.491 --> 00:56:11.701
[beeping]

1273
00:56:15.497 --> 00:56:16.581
[exclaims]

1274
00:56:18.166 --> 00:56:19.626
She's coming to. Buzz.

1275
00:56:19.667 --> 00:56:20.752
[tablet beeping]

1276
00:56:20.794 --> 00:56:21.795
Hurry it up.

1277
00:56:21.836 --> 00:56:23.296
[Buzz] I'm trying. Woody!

1278
00:56:23.338 --> 00:56:25.924
What... What happened?

1279
00:56:25.965 --> 00:56:28.385
Wait. What did you do
to my battery?

1280
00:56:28.426 --> 00:56:29.844
What we'll do again
if you don't tell us

1281
00:56:29.886 --> 00:56:31.429
what happened
to Jessie and Bullseye.

1282
00:56:31.471 --> 00:56:33.306
What time is it? [gasps]

1283
00:56:33.348 --> 00:56:35.225
Oh. no! This is not good.

1284
00:56:35.266 --> 00:56:37.727
The girls got a head start
on Turtle Tag without Bonnie!

1285
00:56:37.769 --> 00:56:39.979
There's been one. two.
three inside jokes already.

1286
00:56:40.021 --> 00:56:41.898
This is a disaster!

1287
00:56:41.940 --> 00:56:43.525
Enough with the silly games.
Where's Jessie and Bullseye?

1288
00:56:43.566 --> 00:56:46.403
Silly? This is serious.
Stuffalo Bill!

1289
00:56:46.444 --> 00:56:47.821
Bonnie is missing out.

1290
00:56:47.862 --> 00:56:49.197
Stuffalo Bill?

1291
00:56:49.239 --> 00:56:50.907
Want her to make friends?
This is how!

1292
00:56:50.949 --> 00:56:53.034
Now keep your little
plastic hands away from me

1293
00:56:53.076 --> 00:56:55.036
or I will set off my alarm.

1294
00:56:55.078 --> 00:56:56.496
I thought you'd say as much.

1295
00:56:56.538 --> 00:56:58.832
Buzz. bring in "Sammy Two."

1296
00:56:58.873 --> 00:57:01.793
-No. No. Absolutely not.
-[grunting]

1297
00:57:02.710 --> 00:57:04.129
-Oh. no. no. no--
-[alarm blaring]

1298
00:57:04.170 --> 00:57:05.588
-[Buzz] Yes. [chuckles]
-[alarm stops]

1299
00:57:05.630 --> 00:57:07.340
-Okay. try "settings."
-You mean this?

1300
00:57:07.382 --> 00:57:09.676
-That's a gear symbol.
-Okay. got it. Now what?

1301
00:57:09.717 --> 00:57:10.760
Reduce her screen time
to zero.

1302
00:57:11.719 --> 00:57:12.804
[Buzz]
The shortest is an hour.

1303
00:57:14.431 --> 00:57:16.057
-What?
-"Horse grill"? Who is that?

1304
00:57:16.099 --> 00:57:18.017
"Horse girl."

1305
00:57:18.059 --> 00:57:20.019
-She's talking about Jessie.
-Well. then open it. [gasps]

1306
00:57:20.061 --> 00:57:21.354
-Whoa!
-[grunting]

1307
00:57:21.396 --> 00:57:22.730
[tablet chimes]

1308
00:57:22.772 --> 00:57:25.024
-[Lilypad exclaims]
-[Woody] My hips.

1309
00:57:25.066 --> 00:57:26.734
Enjoy the garage. suckers!

1310
00:57:26.776 --> 00:57:28.111
-No. no. no! Lily!
-Wait. Hey!

1311
00:57:28.153 --> 00:57:29.112
[gasps]

1312
00:57:29.154 --> 00:57:30.363
Yes. can I help you?

1313
00:57:31.072 --> 00:57:32.449
Huh?

1314
00:57:32.490 --> 00:57:34.492
-Wait a minute. [shushes]
-Fascinating.

1315
00:57:34.534 --> 00:57:37.203
Lily. bring back
that "horse girl" post.

1316
00:57:37.245 --> 00:57:38.455
[distorted buzzing]

1317
00:57:38.496 --> 00:57:39.706
Okay.

1318
00:57:39.747 --> 00:57:42.750
Oh. she has to do
what you say.

1319
00:57:42.792 --> 00:57:45.003
-[screams]
-[gasps. grunts]

1320
00:57:45.044 --> 00:57:46.379
-She's getting away. Buzz!
-Lily!

1321
00:57:46.421 --> 00:57:47.839
-Hey. Lily!
-Hey. stop her!

1322
00:57:47.881 --> 00:57:49.007
-Hey. Lily!
- Yes?

1323
00:57:49.048 --> 00:57:50.884
-Open that post!
- Okay!

1324
00:57:50.925 --> 00:57:52.969
-[gasps] Jessie.
-Bonnie's gotta see this.

1325
00:57:53.011 --> 00:57:55.013
[Buzz] Show her again.
Where is she? Hey. Lily.

1326
00:57:55.054 --> 00:57:56.389
-Hey. Lily!
- Yes?

1327
00:57:56.431 --> 00:57:57.682
-Show the post.
- Can I help you?

1328
00:57:57.724 --> 00:57:58.725
-Share it everywhere!
-Share!

1329
00:57:58.766 --> 00:57:58.933
- Yes!
-Share!

1330
00:57:59.893 --> 00:58:00.935
We did it!

1331
00:58:00.977 --> 00:58:02.020
So. where did it go?

1332
00:58:02.061 --> 00:58:03.104
Lily...

1333
00:58:03.146 --> 00:58:05.023
[all grunting]

1334
00:58:06.191 --> 00:58:07.317
[Lilypad panting]

1335
00:58:07.358 --> 00:58:08.610
-[machine whirring]
-[gasps]

1336
00:58:09.736 --> 00:58:11.779
-[Buzz] The printer! Yes!
-[Woody laughs]

1337
00:58:11.821 --> 00:58:13.406
[Bonnie] Okay. I'm done.

1338
00:58:13.448 --> 00:58:14.741
[Mom] Bonnie. you haven't
finished your breakfast.

1339
00:58:14.782 --> 00:58:15.909
-[Bonnie] No. I'm done.
-[gasps]

1340
00:58:17.410 --> 00:58:20.288
I'm missing Turtle Tag. Mom.
They're playing without me.

1341
00:58:20.330 --> 00:58:22.874
-[groans. pants]
-[Lilypad laughs]

1342
00:58:22.916 --> 00:58:24.292
Now what. Deputy?

1343
00:58:24.334 --> 00:58:26.044
Well.
you're the deputy. Deputy.

1344
00:58:28.505 --> 00:58:30.215
What's this all about. Bonnie?

1345
00:58:32.091 --> 00:58:34.052
-Huh?
-[groans]

1346
00:58:37.138 --> 00:58:39.182
So. why did you put her toys
in the garage?

1347
00:58:39.224 --> 00:58:41.226
Uh. because Bonnie
asked me to.

1348
00:58:41.267 --> 00:58:43.311
-Remember. sweetie?
-No.

1349
00:58:43.353 --> 00:58:45.188
[Dad] Well. I don't think
Lilypad texted me.

1350
00:58:45.230 --> 00:58:48.650
They're gone. She really does
have Jessie and Bullseye.

1351
00:58:48.691 --> 00:58:50.360
I hope they're okay.

1352
00:58:50.401 --> 00:58:52.070
Okay. we've gotten
the queen to safety.

1353
00:58:52.111 --> 00:58:54.781
Yes. You can do this.
Agent Clydesdale.

1354
00:58:54.822 --> 00:58:56.449
One of these buttons
defuses the bomb.

1355
00:58:56.491 --> 00:58:58.451
But which one.
Agent "Sheetland"?

1356
00:58:58.493 --> 00:59:00.620
"Shet"! [sobbing] It's "Shet"!

1357
00:59:00.662 --> 00:59:02.539
[beeping]

1358
00:59:03.122 --> 00:59:04.165
[beeping stops]

1359
00:59:05.792 --> 00:59:07.794
Boom! [imitates explosion]

1360
00:59:07.835 --> 00:59:10.964
Oh. no! [imitates explosion]
[screams]

1361
00:59:11.005 --> 00:59:13.633
[Blaze's mom] Blaze! Hon!
It's time to feed Daffodil.

1362
00:59:13.675 --> 00:59:15.718
[kisses] Okay! [chuckles]

1363
00:59:15.760 --> 00:59:17.637
Come on. Your Majesty.

1364
00:59:18.638 --> 00:59:19.973
[Blaze's mom] Thanks. babe!

1365
00:59:20.014 --> 00:59:21.057
[door closes]

1366
00:59:21.099 --> 00:59:22.642
[Snappy laughs]

1367
00:59:22.684 --> 00:59:24.435
-Holy cow! Wow!
-That was so cool! [squeals]

1368
00:59:24.477 --> 00:59:26.771
-I was a spy! What?
-Yeah. you were!

1369
00:59:26.813 --> 00:59:28.064
-You were the best spy!
-Wow.

1370
00:59:28.106 --> 00:59:29.691
[both chuckling]

1371
00:59:29.732 --> 00:59:31.859
-Smarty?
-[sobbing]

1372
00:59:31.901 --> 00:59:34.529
That was so beautiful.

1373
00:59:34.571 --> 00:59:37.365
That. my friend. was playin'.

1374
00:59:37.407 --> 00:59:39.909
-Oh. boy. did we.
-I feel so alive!

1375
00:59:39.951 --> 00:59:41.911
Is that what being
a toy is like. Sheriff?

1376
00:59:41.953 --> 00:59:43.955
Well. yeah. it's...
Wait. hold up.

1377
00:59:43.997 --> 00:59:46.749
You never called me
sheriff before in a nice way.

1378
00:59:46.791 --> 00:59:48.167
But. well. now I get it.

1379
00:59:48.209 --> 00:59:50.420
Blaze really is perfect
for Bonnie.

1380
00:59:50.461 --> 00:59:52.672
Playing with her
feels just the same.

1381
00:59:52.714 --> 00:59:55.174
-Your kid plays like that too?
-[chimes]

1382
00:59:55.216 --> 00:59:56.259
[all gasp]

1383
00:59:57.927 --> 00:59:59.137
-[Jessie gasps]
-[gasps] It's her!

1384
00:59:59.178 --> 01:00:00.888
She saw the post! It's Bonnie!

1385
01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:02.390
-Go on! Do it.
-Text her back.

1386
01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:03.975
-Go on.
-Text her back.

1387
01:00:04.017 --> 01:00:06.728
[all chanting]
Text her back! Text her back.

1388
01:00:06.769 --> 01:00:09.105
Okay. okay. how do I do that?

1389
01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:11.941
[tablet beeping]

1390
01:00:18.573 --> 01:00:20.658
[beeping]

1391
01:00:24.912 --> 01:00:28.041
-[sighs]
-What? Oh. yes!

1392
01:00:28.082 --> 01:00:29.917
-All right!
-She's coming.

1393
01:00:29.959 --> 01:00:32.253
-Bonnie's coming here.
-[Snappy] I knew she would.

1394
01:00:32.295 --> 01:00:34.505
Blaze and Bonnie
are gonna meet.

1395
01:00:34.547 --> 01:00:36.466
-[beeping]
-Smarty. what are you typing?

1396
01:00:36.507 --> 01:00:38.468
-Delete that right now.
-What?

1397
01:00:38.509 --> 01:00:40.720
I'm just trying to get some
batteries out of the deal.

1398
01:00:42.055 --> 01:00:43.348
So. what's going on?

1399
01:00:43.389 --> 01:00:44.891
Slink. talk to me.

1400
01:00:44.932 --> 01:00:46.809
Hard to hear.
A lot of commotion.

1401
01:00:46.851 --> 01:00:48.603
I bet they're arguing over
getting rid of us.

1402
01:00:48.645 --> 01:00:50.563
[exclaims]
Are we getting donated?

1403
01:00:50.605 --> 01:00:53.691
-Mmm. Doughnuts.
-No. sweetie. Donated.

1404
01:00:53.816 --> 01:00:55.818
Wow. I love her.
but this is gonna be hard.

1405
01:00:55.860 --> 01:00:58.946
Shh! Quiet! I hear something.
Like tiny footsteps.

1406
01:00:58.988 --> 01:01:00.907
-Aw. Kind of cute.
-[footsteps approaching]

1407
01:01:00.948 --> 01:01:02.158
[shouting]

1408
01:01:02.200 --> 01:01:03.826
-Look out!
-Bonnie's coming!

1409
01:01:06.496 --> 01:01:07.830
Come on. Mom.

1410
01:01:07.872 --> 01:01:09.707
[Woody]
Oh. no. Lily's going too.

1411
01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:11.250
[Bonnie's mom] Hold on.
Bonnie. I'm sure your toys

1412
01:01:11.292 --> 01:01:12.752
aren't going to run off
on their own.

1413
01:01:12.794 --> 01:01:14.504
All right. Buzz.
you've gotta stay here.

1414
01:01:14.545 --> 01:01:16.047
-I'm going with them.
-Why? Why just you?

1415
01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:16.798
Look. I just have more
field experience than you.

1416
01:01:16.839 --> 01:01:17.590
That is all.

1417
01:01:18.341 --> 01:01:19.967
You don't think I can do it.

1418
01:01:20.009 --> 01:01:21.928
No. I just think I can do it
a little bit...

1419
01:01:21.969 --> 01:01:24.180
-[car engine starts]
-...better.

1420
01:01:24.222 --> 01:01:26.391
[gasps]
You don't deserve this.

1421
01:01:26.432 --> 01:01:28.601
-Buzz. come on. I was only--
-Jessie put me in charge.

1422
01:01:28.643 --> 01:01:30.853
Which is why you should
stay here and watch the room.

1423
01:01:30.895 --> 01:01:32.647
There is no room
without Jessie.

1424
01:01:32.689 --> 01:01:34.565
Buzz. no! [groans]

1425
01:01:34.607 --> 01:01:37.151
[♪ dramatic music playing]

1426
01:01:37.193 --> 01:01:39.445
[panting. grunting]

1427
01:01:40.446 --> 01:01:42.949
[breathing heavily]

1428
01:01:42.990 --> 01:01:43.950
[grunts]

1429
01:01:43.991 --> 01:01:46.369
Nice poncho. [scoffs]

1430
01:01:46.411 --> 01:01:48.413
It's good
to see them fighting again.

1431
01:01:48.454 --> 01:01:49.664
[Slinky Dog] It sure is.

1432
01:01:56.921 --> 01:01:59.090
How did your toys get
all the way out here?

1433
01:01:59.132 --> 01:02:00.508
[grunts]

1434
01:02:00.550 --> 01:02:01.592
[tablet chirps]

1435
01:02:07.306 --> 01:02:08.975
[gasps]

1436
01:02:15.732 --> 01:02:16.774
[gasps]

1437
01:02:23.865 --> 01:02:27.034
Oh. how 'bout this one?
Ah. look at those puppies.

1438
01:02:27.076 --> 01:02:28.703
I'm saving that one.

1439
01:02:28.745 --> 01:02:30.621
Yeah. they came with the
latest update this morning.

1440
01:02:30.663 --> 01:02:31.914
I know. It never gets old.

1441
01:02:31.956 --> 01:02:33.207
[chuckling] She's here.

1442
01:02:33.249 --> 01:02:35.209
Careful. Snappy.
Dad might see you.

1443
01:02:35.251 --> 01:02:37.920
No way. He'll be showing off
those new backgrounds forever.

1444
01:02:37.962 --> 01:02:40.465
[gasps] That's her!
That's Bonnie!

1445
01:02:40.506 --> 01:02:43.092
-Bullseye. she's really here!
-[blusters]

1446
01:02:44.343 --> 01:02:46.095
Bonnie. come on. let's go.

1447
01:02:50.600 --> 01:02:54.312
[coughs] Buzz. listen.
I really just...

1448
01:02:54.353 --> 01:02:55.605
[Woody groans]

1449
01:02:58.065 --> 01:02:59.358
[Atlas] Aw. [chuckles]

1450
01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.027
It was nothing.
It was nothing.

1451
01:03:01.068 --> 01:03:04.113
Thanks. fellas.
Pretty glad I met you devices.

1452
01:03:04.155 --> 01:03:06.407
Ah. don't be dumping us
something you can't flush.

1453
01:03:06.449 --> 01:03:08.534
-[doorbell rings]
-[gasps] It's her!

1454
01:03:10.828 --> 01:03:12.455
Hello. Can I help you?

1455
01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:14.916
Hi. I'm so sorry
to bother you.

1456
01:03:14.957 --> 01:03:17.001
but we got this message
from your daughter.

1457
01:03:17.043 --> 01:03:19.462
She seems to have found
my daughter's toys.

1458
01:03:19.504 --> 01:03:21.047
-Are they in there?
-[Blaze's mom] Oh. okay.

1459
01:03:21.088 --> 01:03:22.423
I'll have her get 'em.

1460
01:03:22.465 --> 01:03:24.342
-Blaze! Honey?
-[Blaze] Yeah?

1461
01:03:24.383 --> 01:03:26.803
Can you bring down
those two rag dolls you found?

1462
01:03:26.844 --> 01:03:29.096
-Their owner's here.
-[Blaze] Okay!

1463
01:03:29.138 --> 01:03:31.474
-That's our cue.
-[footsteps approaching]

1464
01:03:41.150 --> 01:03:42.193
[gasps]

1465
01:03:42.235 --> 01:03:44.737
Blaze. this is. uh...

1466
01:03:44.779 --> 01:03:46.239
[Bonnie's mom] This is Bonnie.

1467
01:03:46.280 --> 01:03:47.323
[Blaze's mom] Hello. Bonnie.

1468
01:03:47.365 --> 01:03:49.367
Hi. Are these your toys?

1469
01:03:56.332 --> 01:03:58.376
I don't play
with toys anymore.

1470
01:03:58.417 --> 01:04:01.712
It's just they're antiques.

1471
01:04:04.131 --> 01:04:06.342
They do look pretty old.

1472
01:04:06.384 --> 01:04:08.719
Must be worth something
at least. right?

1473
01:04:10.805 --> 01:04:12.014
No. they're not.

1474
01:04:13.224 --> 01:04:14.517
You should keep 'em.

1475
01:04:17.144 --> 01:04:18.271
[both gasp]

1476
01:04:18.312 --> 01:04:19.730
-[gasps]
-Oh. no.

1477
01:04:21.190 --> 01:04:23.109
Bonnie. you don't want them?

1478
01:04:28.364 --> 01:04:31.742
[stammers] Are you sure?
Bonnie? Bonnie?

1479
01:04:32.660 --> 01:04:34.078
I don't know
what's come over her.

1480
01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:35.830
I'm so sorry
to have bothered you.

1481
01:04:35.872 --> 01:04:37.582
It's all right.

1482
01:04:37.623 --> 01:04:40.167
If you ever change your mind.
Bonnie. just let me know.

1483
01:04:40.209 --> 01:04:42.420
[♪ mournful music playing]

1484
01:04:48.551 --> 01:04:50.011
[door closes]

1485
01:04:50.052 --> 01:04:51.178
I don't get it.
What just happened?

1486
01:04:51.220 --> 01:04:52.722
What is going on. Bonnie?

1487
01:04:53.890 --> 01:04:55.182
Okay. I guess we're going.

1488
01:04:56.142 --> 01:04:58.477
-[sniffles]
-[car door opens. closes]

1489
01:05:01.522 --> 01:05:03.608
[all gasp. grunt]

1490
01:05:03.649 --> 01:05:05.067
[footsteps approaching]

1491
01:05:12.783 --> 01:05:14.243
[door creaks]

1492
01:05:15.494 --> 01:05:17.079
[gasps]

1493
01:05:17.121 --> 01:05:19.790
Come on. Bullseye! Quick!
Before they drive away!

1494
01:05:19.832 --> 01:05:21.000
[grunting]

1495
01:05:21.751 --> 01:05:23.252
It's... It's too late for me.

1496
01:05:23.294 --> 01:05:25.254
Bullseye.
but maybe not for you.

1497
01:05:25.296 --> 01:05:26.923
-Please. not for you.
-[blusters]

1498
01:05:26.964 --> 01:05:30.426
[grunts. breathing heavily]

1499
01:05:31.218 --> 01:05:32.511
-[whinnies]
-[Jessie sighs]

1500
01:05:34.680 --> 01:05:37.224
-Sheriff?
-Jessie? A-Are you okay?

1501
01:05:37.266 --> 01:05:38.726
W-What just happened?

1502
01:05:38.768 --> 01:05:40.311
She ditched you. Jessie.

1503
01:05:40.353 --> 01:05:41.938
Because of you!

1504
01:05:41.979 --> 01:05:44.273
Because of all you
darn devices

1505
01:05:44.315 --> 01:05:46.150
making kids act older.

1506
01:05:46.192 --> 01:05:48.194
You stole all our time.

1507
01:05:48.235 --> 01:05:51.072
I wanted to make a difference.
I needed to make a difference.

1508
01:05:51.113 --> 01:05:52.490
And you ruined it.

1509
01:05:52.531 --> 01:05:54.033
-Ow.
-[gasps]

1510
01:05:54.075 --> 01:05:56.118
-Smarty. you okay?
-I'm-I'm sorry.

1511
01:05:56.160 --> 01:05:59.038
-Are you hurt? Did you crack?
-I'm fine. I'm fine. [sighs]

1512
01:05:59.080 --> 01:06:01.207
For a rag doll. you throw
quite a punch. cowgir...

1513
01:06:02.041 --> 01:06:03.459
Cowgirl?

1514
01:06:04.794 --> 01:06:06.462
-[devices gasp]
-[Bullseye whinnies]

1515
01:06:06.504 --> 01:06:07.588
[Snappy] Jessie?

1516
01:06:14.178 --> 01:06:15.763
[whistles]

1517
01:06:17.390 --> 01:06:19.100
Uh. Sheriff?

1518
01:06:19.141 --> 01:06:20.851
I'm sorry. Smarty.

1519
01:06:20.893 --> 01:06:22.144
It's not you.

1520
01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:25.189
I'm the one that's useless.

1521
01:06:25.231 --> 01:06:26.607
-[devices gasp]
-[blusters]

1522
01:06:29.527 --> 01:06:30.569
[whinnies]

1523
01:06:37.618 --> 01:06:38.953
[gasps] Bullseye!

1524
01:06:41.455 --> 01:06:44.083
Poor Jessie.
Gotta find a way in.

1525
01:06:45.418 --> 01:06:48.087
Buzz. Buzz.
where are you going?

1526
01:06:48.129 --> 01:06:50.172
Let's talk about this.
[groans]

1527
01:06:50.214 --> 01:06:51.966
-[electronic wailing]
-Huh?

1528
01:06:53.759 --> 01:06:56.345
Uh. what... what is going on?

1529
01:06:56.387 --> 01:06:57.847
-State your name.
-[Woody] Whoa. whoa.

1530
01:06:57.888 --> 01:06:59.724
-And your purpose.
-Hey. guys. [stammers]

1531
01:06:59.765 --> 01:07:01.517
-Take him in.
-Guys! Whoa!

1532
01:07:02.143 --> 01:07:03.936
[groaning]

1533
01:07:03.978 --> 01:07:04.979
-Wait. wait. What's going on?
-[Jimmy Dean snorting]

1534
01:07:05.021 --> 01:07:06.689
[screams] My poncho!

1535
01:07:07.189 --> 01:07:08.566
Quiet. assassin!

1536
01:07:08.607 --> 01:07:10.985
[grunts] Assassin?
No. I can't...

1537
01:07:11.027 --> 01:07:12.153
[straining]

1538
01:07:12.194 --> 01:07:13.738
-Buzz?
-[all gasp]

1539
01:07:13.779 --> 01:07:15.865
How do you know who we are?
Who sent you?

1540
01:07:15.906 --> 01:07:18.117
[Woody] Oh. geez! What... I...

1541
01:07:18.159 --> 01:07:20.244
-Talk!
-[screams]

1542
01:07:20.286 --> 01:07:22.079
-[snorting]
-Talk about what?

1543
01:07:22.121 --> 01:07:24.165
-What am I supposed to know?
-You bear a holster.

1544
01:07:24.206 --> 01:07:27.168
You were positioned outside
our leader's stronghold.

1545
01:07:27.209 --> 01:07:29.003
You are an agent of Zurg!

1546
01:07:29.045 --> 01:07:30.588
Zurg? No! Hey!

1547
01:07:30.629 --> 01:07:32.173
I don't even know
who your leader is!

1548
01:07:32.214 --> 01:07:34.717
Liar! You wish to harm
the red-haired maiden

1549
01:07:34.759 --> 01:07:36.218
who bears the mark
of Star Command.

1550
01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:37.511
-Jessie.
-[Woody] No.

1551
01:07:37.553 --> 01:07:39.263
-Wait!
-[Woody grunting]

1552
01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:41.390
He is not an agent of Zurg.

1553
01:07:41.432 --> 01:07:42.808
[all muttering]

1554
01:07:42.850 --> 01:07:44.185
Well. then.
who's this old man?

1555
01:07:44.226 --> 01:07:45.853
[stammers] Why do people
keep saying that?

1556
01:07:45.895 --> 01:07:46.896
I'm not that old!

1557
01:07:46.937 --> 01:07:49.815
This old man is a toy.

1558
01:07:49.857 --> 01:07:51.692
Hmm. A toy?

1559
01:07:52.318 --> 01:07:54.695
Yes. We are all toys!

1560
01:07:54.737 --> 01:07:56.447
-Toy...
-[clamoring]

1561
01:07:56.489 --> 01:07:58.866
Our mission on this planet is
to make a child happy.

1562
01:07:58.908 --> 01:07:59.992
I've been dreaming about that.

1563
01:08:00.034 --> 01:08:01.202
You know what I mean?

1564
01:08:01.243 --> 01:08:03.370
-[Buzz] To play!
-To play. Play.

1565
01:08:03.412 --> 01:08:04.747
Hey! Buzz. can you help me...

1566
01:08:04.789 --> 01:08:06.499
[muffled] ...get out
of the mouth of this pig?

1567
01:08:06.540 --> 01:08:09.960
Search your feelings. Buzz.
You know it to be true!

1568
01:08:10.002 --> 01:08:12.588
-[Woody groaning]
-[clamoring]

1569
01:08:12.630 --> 01:08:15.883
And the red-haired maiden
you seek is our toy leader.

1570
01:08:15.925 --> 01:08:17.885
Her name is Sheriff Jessie.

1571
01:08:17.927 --> 01:08:19.512
[all] Sheriff Jessie.

1572
01:08:19.553 --> 01:08:22.223
Sheriff Jessie is trapped
inside that stronghold.

1573
01:08:22.264 --> 01:08:24.433
We must infiltrate it
and rescue her

1574
01:08:24.475 --> 01:08:25.684
and her trusty steed.

1575
01:08:25.726 --> 01:08:27.019
How do you know all this?

1576
01:08:27.686 --> 01:08:30.064
Because I am her deputy.

1577
01:08:30.106 --> 01:08:31.565
[♪ triumphant music playing]

1578
01:08:31.607 --> 01:08:33.025
[all] Star Command.

1579
01:08:33.067 --> 01:08:36.237
Then this old man is a toy?

1580
01:08:36.278 --> 01:08:38.114
[muffled]
This pig has bad breath!

1581
01:08:38.155 --> 01:08:39.532
Oh. yeah. him.

1582
01:08:39.573 --> 01:08:41.408
He's my sidekick.
You can untie him.

1583
01:08:41.450 --> 01:08:45.329
And by the way. everybody.
Zurg is our dad.

1584
01:08:45.371 --> 01:08:48.499
-[all] No! No! [sobbing]
-Yeah.

1585
01:08:50.668 --> 01:08:52.711
[♪ adventurous music playing]

1586
01:08:55.631 --> 01:08:57.883
Hey. What's on your mind?

1587
01:08:57.925 --> 01:08:59.093
[Blaze] I don't know.

1588
01:08:59.135 --> 01:09:00.678
I just hope that girl's okay.

1589
01:09:00.719 --> 01:09:03.305
[Blaze's mom] Aw.
She'll be fine. sweetie.

1590
01:09:03.347 --> 01:09:04.515
-Don't you worry.
-[door opens]

1591
01:09:04.557 --> 01:09:06.767
Hey. guys! Is anyone hungry?

1592
01:09:06.809 --> 01:09:08.227
-[Blaze] Me. me!
-[Blaze's mom] Starving!

1593
01:09:08.269 --> 01:09:10.187
[Blaze] Can we get
Pasta Prairie. Baba?

1594
01:09:10.229 --> 01:09:12.356
[Blaze's dad] Ooh. I like
the way you think. anushikes .

1595
01:09:14.525 --> 01:09:16.777
-[panting]
-Spread out.

1596
01:09:17.444 --> 01:09:18.571
Not here.

1597
01:09:19.113 --> 01:09:20.406
Not here.

1598
01:09:20.447 --> 01:09:21.490
Definitely not here.

1599
01:09:22.283 --> 01:09:23.909
Blast! Where could she be?

1600
01:09:23.951 --> 01:09:26.412
Commander! We found
these electronic devices.

1601
01:09:26.453 --> 01:09:29.540
Hey. Micro-Chippendales!
Hands off. [groans]

1602
01:09:29.582 --> 01:09:31.333
-[chimes]
-Whoa!

1603
01:09:31.375 --> 01:09:33.377
I'm getting a major signal
from all you dudes.

1604
01:09:33.419 --> 01:09:36.255
-I've got full bars.
-Me too. I can map for miles!

1605
01:09:36.297 --> 01:09:38.174
These guys
are their own hot spot.

1606
01:09:38.215 --> 01:09:39.633
[beeping]

1607
01:09:39.675 --> 01:09:40.968
Oh. no. They're one of them.

1608
01:09:41.010 --> 01:09:43.762
They're one of us! Nice.

1609
01:09:43.804 --> 01:09:45.264
Hey. uh. this one's broken.
by the way.

1610
01:09:45.306 --> 01:09:47.057
Where are you hiding Jessie.
you machine?

1611
01:09:47.099 --> 01:09:48.642
Hey. hey. Easy there.

1612
01:09:48.684 --> 01:09:50.269
-Yeah!
-We're Jessie's friends!

1613
01:09:50.311 --> 01:09:52.771
And I have a name.
It's Smarty Pants.

1614
01:09:52.813 --> 01:09:54.023
Hygiene instructor.

1615
01:09:54.064 --> 01:09:55.232
He'll wipe your--

1616
01:09:55.274 --> 01:09:57.318
This is serious. Mr. Pants.

1617
01:09:57.359 --> 01:09:59.278
It is my sworn duty
as a Space Ranger--

1618
01:09:59.320 --> 01:10:01.405
-Ha. ha. you said "doody."
-Why. you!

1619
01:10:01.447 --> 01:10:03.115
Clearly. we're all friends
with Jessie.

1620
01:10:03.157 --> 01:10:04.992
so can you just tell us
where she is?

1621
01:10:05.034 --> 01:10:06.493
She went
to the tire-swing hill!

1622
01:10:06.535 --> 01:10:07.912
It's at the far end
of the ranch.

1623
01:10:07.953 --> 01:10:09.455
Gonna take me forever
to waddle there.

1624
01:10:09.496 --> 01:10:12.041
Well. we'll need a way
to get there.

1625
01:10:12.082 --> 01:10:13.334
[Buzz Lightyears]
Commander Lightyear.

1626
01:10:13.375 --> 01:10:15.419
[♪ uplifting music playing]

1627
01:10:15.461 --> 01:10:16.795
-[gasps]
-Oh. my.

1628
01:10:19.548 --> 01:10:20.841
Whoa.

1629
01:10:30.351 --> 01:10:33.020
Bonnie? Did something happen
with your friends?

1630
01:10:38.400 --> 01:10:39.443
Can you show me?

1631
01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:43.989
You're not in trouble. Bonnie.
I promise.

1632
01:10:52.831 --> 01:10:54.625
Oh. sweetie.

1633
01:10:54.667 --> 01:10:58.087
You know that you can always
talk with me and Dad. right?

1634
01:10:58.587 --> 01:11:00.422
About anything.

1635
01:11:00.464 --> 01:11:03.509
Because we love you.
Bonnie. so much.

1636
01:11:04.593 --> 01:11:08.013
I wouldn't change
a single thing about you.

1637
01:11:08.055 --> 01:11:10.933
And I think a real friend
would feel the same.

1638
01:11:10.975 --> 01:11:12.017
Don't you?

1639
01:11:13.310 --> 01:11:14.645
But how about we take a break

1640
01:11:14.687 --> 01:11:16.438
from the group chat
for now. Okay?

1641
01:11:17.147 --> 01:11:18.399
Let's get some ice cream.

1642
01:11:19.775 --> 01:11:21.318
[sobs]

1643
01:11:27.574 --> 01:11:29.285
Trust me.
you're gonna love it.

1644
01:11:29.326 --> 01:11:30.452
[chuckling]

1645
01:11:30.494 --> 01:11:31.745
-Cool! [chuckling]
-Sure.

1646
01:11:34.957 --> 01:11:36.000
[chuckling continues]

1647
01:11:43.382 --> 01:11:46.093
Bonnie. they don't have
chocolate chip.

1648
01:11:46.135 --> 01:11:47.761
Come pick another flavor.

1649
01:11:49.013 --> 01:11:51.640
[grunting]

1650
01:11:54.727 --> 01:11:56.186
[panting]

1651
01:12:07.031 --> 01:12:09.325
-[door closes]
-[engine starts]

1652
01:12:09.366 --> 01:12:12.161
-Mom. where's Lilypad?
-[Lilypad panting]

1653
01:12:12.202 --> 01:12:13.954
I'm sorry. Bonnie.

1654
01:12:22.171 --> 01:12:23.505
[creaks]

1655
01:12:31.555 --> 01:12:33.140
[sighs]

1656
01:12:33.182 --> 01:12:34.600
-[♪ suspenseful music plays]
-[grass rustling]

1657
01:12:34.641 --> 01:12:36.101
-[blusters]
-What is it?

1658
01:12:36.143 --> 01:12:37.811
-[♪ triumphant music plays]
-[nickers]

1659
01:12:38.604 --> 01:12:39.605
-[shouts]
-[music ends]

1660
01:12:39.646 --> 01:12:40.981
[grunts] Bullseye.

1661
01:12:41.023 --> 01:12:42.608
You shouldn't have
followed me.

1662
01:12:42.649 --> 01:12:45.277
-[nickers]
-Oh. bad horse.

1663
01:12:45.986 --> 01:12:46.820
[blusters]

1664
01:12:47.488 --> 01:12:49.365
[sighs]

1665
01:12:49.406 --> 01:12:52.326
You go back to Blaze's.
Bullseye. You're better off.

1666
01:12:52.368 --> 01:12:54.536
-[♪ somber music plays]
-[whinnies. blusters]

1667
01:12:54.578 --> 01:12:58.040
I'm serious.
She'll take good care of you.

1668
01:12:58.082 --> 01:12:59.583
And all those horses...

1669
01:12:59.625 --> 01:13:01.043
[blusters]

1670
01:13:01.085 --> 01:13:02.127
[whinnies]

1671
01:13:03.295 --> 01:13:05.339
[sighs] Bullseye. no.

1672
01:13:05.381 --> 01:13:07.049
I'm not going with you.

1673
01:13:07.549 --> 01:13:09.218
I...

1674
01:13:09.259 --> 01:13:11.387
can't do this again.

1675
01:13:11.428 --> 01:13:12.471
I can't...

1676
01:13:13.597 --> 01:13:15.224
love another kid

1677
01:13:15.265 --> 01:13:17.976
just to find out
I never mattered.

1678
01:13:19.645 --> 01:13:20.521
I...

1679
01:13:21.271 --> 01:13:22.940
I can't.

1680
01:13:25.609 --> 01:13:27.945
[blusters]

1681
01:13:30.322 --> 01:13:31.615
[♪ uplifting music plays]

1682
01:13:40.833 --> 01:13:43.544
-[blusters]
-I didn't write that.

1683
01:13:44.378 --> 01:13:45.921
It must have been...

1684
01:14:01.395 --> 01:14:02.396
[gasps]

1685
01:14:02.438 --> 01:14:03.647
Emily?

1686
01:14:04.857 --> 01:14:06.483
[Jessie whistles]

1687
01:14:06.525 --> 01:14:09.069
-Daffodil. dig.
-[whinnies]

1688
01:14:09.111 --> 01:14:10.404
[blusters]

1689
01:14:13.615 --> 01:14:14.658
[blusters]

1690
01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:16.535
[music continues]

1691
01:14:23.041 --> 01:14:24.126
[lock clicks]

1692
01:14:24.168 --> 01:14:26.003
[♪ melancholy music plays]

1693
01:14:26.044 --> 01:14:27.129
Wait.

1694
01:14:28.338 --> 01:14:30.466
This ain't stuff from Emily.

1695
01:14:30.507 --> 01:14:31.550
It...

1696
01:14:32.134 --> 01:14:33.302
It's newer.

1697
01:14:35.971 --> 01:14:37.347
It doesn't make any sense.

1698
01:14:37.389 --> 01:14:39.391
She wouldn't have
any of this stuff.

1699
01:14:39.433 --> 01:14:40.976
She'd be...

1700
01:14:44.271 --> 01:14:46.064
all grown-up.

1701
01:14:46.106 --> 01:14:47.983
[♪ uplifting music plays]

1702
01:14:49.485 --> 01:14:50.527
Wait.

1703
01:14:57.326 --> 01:15:00.162
Emily named her daughter...

1704
01:15:04.041 --> 01:15:05.501
after me.

1705
01:15:15.302 --> 01:15:16.678
Really?

1706
01:15:18.639 --> 01:15:20.057
[blusters]

1707
01:15:21.683 --> 01:15:22.726
[nickers]

1708
01:15:24.269 --> 01:15:25.854
[music continues]

1709
01:15:29.107 --> 01:15:30.901
-[grass rustling]
-[blusters]

1710
01:15:30.943 --> 01:15:32.277
-[whinnies]
-[♪ dramatic music plays]

1711
01:15:32.319 --> 01:15:33.695
Uh...

1712
01:15:33.737 --> 01:15:35.656
[screams] Whoa!

1713
01:15:35.697 --> 01:15:37.157
[groans]

1714
01:15:37.199 --> 01:15:38.534
[breathing heavily]

1715
01:15:40.285 --> 01:15:42.037
Jessie? Bullseye!

1716
01:15:42.079 --> 01:15:42.955
-Hey. I found 'em!
-[♪ triumphant music plays]

1717
01:15:42.996 --> 01:15:44.081
Woody?

1718
01:15:44.998 --> 01:15:46.750
-Buzz!
-Jessie!

1719
01:15:46.792 --> 01:15:47.709
[grunts]

1720
01:15:47.751 --> 01:15:48.961
You're okay.

1721
01:15:49.002 --> 01:15:50.963
What...
What are you doing here?

1722
01:15:51.004 --> 01:15:52.589
We came for you. Jessie.

1723
01:15:52.631 --> 01:15:53.715
For me?

1724
01:15:53.757 --> 01:15:55.259
We all did.

1725
01:16:03.934 --> 01:16:06.853
Well. howdy-do. Sheriff?

1726
01:16:06.895 --> 01:16:08.480
We come bearing Buzzes.

1727
01:16:08.522 --> 01:16:10.691
Looks like 50 to me.
but I can only count to two.

1728
01:16:10.732 --> 01:16:11.692
[gasps]

1729
01:16:13.026 --> 01:16:15.404
Star Command. Star Command.
Star Command. Star Command.

1730
01:16:15.445 --> 01:16:17.489
Star Command.
Star Command. Star Command.

1731
01:16:18.031 --> 01:16:19.408
Star Command.

1732
01:16:19.449 --> 01:16:21.535
All right.
all right. calm down.

1733
01:16:21.577 --> 01:16:22.744
Give her some room. fellas.

1734
01:16:22.786 --> 01:16:24.788
-Uh. Buzz.
-Yes?

1735
01:16:24.830 --> 01:16:28.041
Hey. hey. she meant that
for me. Just me.

1736
01:16:28.083 --> 01:16:30.377
-We saw Bonnie give you away.
-You did?

1737
01:16:30.419 --> 01:16:31.878
It doesn't make any sense.

1738
01:16:31.920 --> 01:16:33.213
You're not useless. Sheriff!

1739
01:16:33.255 --> 01:16:35.299
-We love you!
-So much!

1740
01:16:35.340 --> 01:16:36.758
[Atlas sobbing]

1741
01:16:36.800 --> 01:16:38.468
[♪ melancholy music plays]

1742
01:16:43.181 --> 01:16:44.600
Look. I'm okay.

1743
01:16:45.225 --> 01:16:47.978
Bonnie's growing up.

1744
01:16:49.187 --> 01:16:54.276
And we don't get to decide
when and how that happens.

1745
01:16:55.485 --> 01:16:56.945
All that matters is

1746
01:16:56.987 --> 01:16:58.989
we were there
at the right time

1747
01:16:59.031 --> 01:17:00.741
to help her along.

1748
01:17:00.782 --> 01:17:01.825
[blusters]

1749
01:17:07.581 --> 01:17:09.708
And I gotta believe we were.

1750
01:17:10.834 --> 01:17:12.919
You make us proud to be toys.
Jessie.

1751
01:17:12.961 --> 01:17:14.546
-What are you doing? Stop!
-[groaning]

1752
01:17:14.588 --> 01:17:16.632
[clears throat]
Sorry. guys. Sorry.

1753
01:17:16.673 --> 01:17:18.300
[blusters]

1754
01:17:18.342 --> 01:17:20.719
Just wish she had at least
connected with Blaze.

1755
01:17:21.637 --> 01:17:23.263
Wait.

1756
01:17:23.305 --> 01:17:25.182
-Connect! They still can!
-[♪ upbeat music plays]

1757
01:17:25.223 --> 01:17:26.767
Lilypad can do that!

1758
01:17:26.808 --> 01:17:28.101
-Lilypad?
-Lilypad?

1759
01:17:29.853 --> 01:17:31.647
-[grunts]
-[beeps]

1760
01:17:36.526 --> 01:17:38.236
Okay. okay.
Guys. message coming through.

1761
01:17:38.278 --> 01:17:40.238
"Jessie. I'm so sorry.

1762
01:17:40.280 --> 01:17:42.324
Chose wrong friends.
Hurt Bonnie."

1763
01:17:42.366 --> 01:17:43.742
-Oh. no.
-Bonnie.

1764
01:17:43.784 --> 01:17:46.161
Smarty. send a reply.
"You can fix it."

1765
01:17:49.706 --> 01:17:51.500
-[beeps]
-[gasps]

1766
01:17:51.541 --> 01:17:54.211
"No. I can't.
Threw myself away."

1767
01:17:54.252 --> 01:17:56.004
-What?
-"On donation truck."

1768
01:17:56.046 --> 01:17:59.341
Jumpin' Jehoshaphat!
Now she throws herself away?

1769
01:17:59.383 --> 01:18:01.218
[groans]
We're goin' after her.

1770
01:18:01.259 --> 01:18:02.761
-What?
-But how?

1771
01:18:02.803 --> 01:18:05.931
Smarty. tell Lily to send
a photo of where she is.

1772
01:18:06.640 --> 01:18:08.058
Got it.

1773
01:18:08.100 --> 01:18:09.643
Snappy. zoom in
on that blurry road sign.

1774
01:18:09.685 --> 01:18:11.520
Look at you
with that tech talk. cowgirl.

1775
01:18:11.561 --> 01:18:12.896
Martin Avenue.

1776
01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:14.356
Atlas. can you get us
to that truck?

1777
01:18:14.398 --> 01:18:16.274
Already mapped it.
cowboy lady.

1778
01:18:16.316 --> 01:18:18.652
Tell Lily to keep sending
photos of where she is.

1779
01:18:18.694 --> 01:18:20.070
We're getting her back.

1780
01:18:20.112 --> 01:18:21.488
Yes. Sheriff.

1781
01:18:21.530 --> 01:18:23.115
Jessie. when you have
a moment.

1782
01:18:23.156 --> 01:18:24.741
there's something
you'd like to ask me...

1783
01:18:24.783 --> 01:18:26.535
-I'd like to ask you.
-Sure thing. Deputy.

1784
01:18:26.576 --> 01:18:28.578
-Now. a little help?
-Yes. Sheriff.

1785
01:18:29.746 --> 01:18:31.540
Yeehaw!

1786
01:18:31.581 --> 01:18:33.083
Let's ride.

1787
01:18:33.125 --> 01:18:34.418
[♪ triumphant music plays]

1788
01:18:34.459 --> 01:18:36.253
Whoa! Hey!

1789
01:18:38.797 --> 01:18:40.549
-Hey! Hey. wait for us!
-Hey! Wait for us!

1790
01:18:40.590 --> 01:18:41.633
[screams]

1791
01:18:41.675 --> 01:18:42.884
-[squeaking]
-[grunts]

1792
01:18:46.555 --> 01:18:47.681
[grunts]

1793
01:18:47.723 --> 01:18:48.849
[breathing heavily]

1794
01:18:49.641 --> 01:18:50.517
[beeps]

1795
01:18:54.354 --> 01:18:56.189
-[music continues]
-She's not far.

1796
01:18:56.231 --> 01:18:59.151
If we go south five blocks.
then east for two.

1797
01:18:59.192 --> 01:19:00.360
we might be able
to head 'em off

1798
01:19:00.402 --> 01:19:01.069
before they reach
the highway.

1799
01:19:01.111 --> 01:19:02.154
Car!

1800
01:19:02.195 --> 01:19:03.321
[music stops]

1801
01:19:05.490 --> 01:19:07.617
-Clear!
-[music resumes]

1802
01:19:07.659 --> 01:19:08.910
She just passed a gas station.

1803
01:19:08.952 --> 01:19:11.163
[laughs]
Passed gas. Sorry. had to.

1804
01:19:11.204 --> 01:19:12.789
We're close. Take a shortcut.

1805
01:19:12.831 --> 01:19:14.207
Down this next road
to the right.

1806
01:19:17.210 --> 01:19:18.378
-[squeaks]
-[grunts]

1807
01:19:19.379 --> 01:19:20.922
It's a house!

1808
01:19:20.964 --> 01:19:22.424
I don't get it.
There should be a road.

1809
01:19:22.466 --> 01:19:24.176
Probably was a road
five years ago. Old map.

1810
01:19:24.217 --> 01:19:26.344
-Recalculating.
-No time. We're going through.

1811
01:19:26.386 --> 01:19:27.971
-[Buzz] Wait. what?
-[Woody] Going through?

1812
01:19:28.597 --> 01:19:29.931
[music continues]

1813
01:19:36.730 --> 01:19:37.731
[Smarty] Down. boy. down!

1814
01:19:38.482 --> 01:19:39.733
[Woody screams]

1815
01:19:39.775 --> 01:19:41.443
-[screams]
-[Buzz] Whoa. whoa.

1816
01:19:41.485 --> 01:19:42.778
-[Woody grunts]
-[dog barks]

1817
01:19:43.820 --> 01:19:45.071
[barking]

1818
01:19:45.113 --> 01:19:46.490
-Yeehaw!
-[screams]

1819
01:19:46.531 --> 01:19:48.241
-[chicken squawks]
-[Jessie screams]

1820
01:19:48.283 --> 01:19:49.493
[squawking]

1821
01:19:49.534 --> 01:19:50.577
[music continues]

1822
01:19:50.619 --> 01:19:51.745
[coughs]

1823
01:19:52.788 --> 01:19:53.830
[chuckles]

1824
01:19:55.874 --> 01:19:56.958
[shutter clicks]

1825
01:19:57.000 --> 01:20:00.045
The truck. I see it up ahead.

1826
01:20:00.086 --> 01:20:01.546
-[beeping]
-[♪ dramatic music plays]

1827
01:20:01.588 --> 01:20:02.881
Follow me.

1828
01:20:02.923 --> 01:20:04.049
[Buzzes] Yes. Sheriff.

1829
01:20:10.847 --> 01:20:12.933
-[screams]
-[squeaks]

1830
01:20:12.974 --> 01:20:14.184
[Atlas] Whoo!

1831
01:20:14.226 --> 01:20:15.936
We have reached
our destination.

1832
01:20:15.977 --> 01:20:17.354
-Lily?
-Lily!

1833
01:20:17.395 --> 01:20:19.105
-Lily. where are ya?
-[Smarty] Lily!

1834
01:20:19.147 --> 01:20:20.690
-[Jessie] Lily?
-Lilypad. where you at?

1835
01:20:20.732 --> 01:20:21.983
Hey. Lily.

1836
01:20:22.025 --> 01:20:23.318
Yes. can I help you?

1837
01:20:24.820 --> 01:20:27.781
Lily. It's okay. We got ya.

1838
01:20:27.823 --> 01:20:29.282
You shouldn't have come.
Jessie.

1839
01:20:29.324 --> 01:20:31.159
Nuh-uh. No time
for pity parties. Lily.

1840
01:20:31.243 --> 01:20:33.411
Bonnie still needs you
to make a friend.

1841
01:20:33.453 --> 01:20:35.372
Me? But I...

1842
01:20:35.413 --> 01:20:38.750
I made a major miscalculation
with Kara. Chelsea and Heidi.

1843
01:20:38.792 --> 01:20:40.669
You were right.
Bonnie's different.

1844
01:20:40.710 --> 01:20:41.628
She deserves better.

1845
01:20:41.670 --> 01:20:43.421
Lily.

1846
01:20:43.463 --> 01:20:45.131
You didn't know those girls
were wrong for Bonnie.

1847
01:20:45.173 --> 01:20:47.092
No. I'm wrong for Bonnie.

1848
01:20:47.133 --> 01:20:49.761
-I'm the one who caused this.
-Well. then help me fix it.

1849
01:20:49.803 --> 01:20:52.013
I found Bonnie
the right friend.

1850
01:20:52.055 --> 01:20:53.390
-You did?
-Yep.

1851
01:20:53.431 --> 01:20:55.475
So. how about you and me
connect them?

1852
01:20:55.517 --> 01:20:57.394
Uh... Okay.

1853
01:20:57.435 --> 01:20:59.604
But first. we gotta get
everyone off this truck

1854
01:20:59.646 --> 01:21:00.730
and back home.

1855
01:21:00.772 --> 01:21:01.773
[screaming]

1856
01:21:01.815 --> 01:21:03.024
[music continues]

1857
01:21:03.859 --> 01:21:05.652
-[horn honks]
-[grunts]

1858
01:21:05.694 --> 01:21:08.321
Uh. we are moving way too fast
to get off now.

1859
01:21:08.363 --> 01:21:10.824
And we're going farther away
by the second.

1860
01:21:10.866 --> 01:21:12.826
There's gotta be
something we can do.

1861
01:21:12.868 --> 01:21:15.036
We've got all these
fancy Buzzes.

1862
01:21:15.078 --> 01:21:16.288
[gasps]

1863
01:21:17.747 --> 01:21:19.499
Excuse me.
Move. move. Out of the way.

1864
01:21:19.541 --> 01:21:20.834
Spaceman. turn around.

1865
01:21:29.009 --> 01:21:31.469
-Snap!
-[gasps] Yes. yes. yes. yes!

1866
01:21:31.511 --> 01:21:32.846
No way.

1867
01:21:32.888 --> 01:21:34.890
Oh. yeah. Way.

1868
01:21:34.931 --> 01:21:36.600
[♪ triumphant music plays]

1869
01:21:39.603 --> 01:21:40.812
Ready. Sheriff?

1870
01:21:40.854 --> 01:21:42.105
Punch it. Lily.

1871
01:21:43.189 --> 01:21:44.900
[electrical humming]

1872
01:21:48.612 --> 01:21:49.654
[radio beeps]

1873
01:21:49.696 --> 01:21:50.822
[whirring]

1874
01:21:56.536 --> 01:21:58.413
Whoa.

1875
01:21:58.455 --> 01:22:00.582
Fly. Be free!

1876
01:22:00.624 --> 01:22:01.666
Show-offs!

1877
01:22:09.341 --> 01:22:11.134
[laughs] Wow.

1878
01:22:11.176 --> 01:22:12.636
Whoo-hoo!

1879
01:22:13.178 --> 01:22:14.554
-Whoo!
-Whoo!

1880
01:22:15.138 --> 01:22:16.181
[laughs]

1881
01:22:16.222 --> 01:22:18.266
Now. this is flying.

1882
01:22:18.308 --> 01:22:19.476
With style!

1883
01:22:19.517 --> 01:22:22.228
Yeehaw!

1884
01:22:27.484 --> 01:22:29.194
So. we're clear on the plan?

1885
01:22:29.235 --> 01:22:31.112
Once you're at Bonnie's.
you send the message.

1886
01:22:31.154 --> 01:22:33.114
Blaze brings me and Bullseye
to the house.

1887
01:22:33.156 --> 01:22:35.492
and this time. they connect!

1888
01:22:35.533 --> 01:22:37.702
Jessie. wait. What if Bonnie
rejects you again?

1889
01:22:37.744 --> 01:22:40.413
If they become friends.
it's all worth it.

1890
01:22:40.455 --> 01:22:41.998
Yes. Sheriff.

1891
01:22:43.083 --> 01:22:46.086
Huh? Wait. Jessie. wait!

1892
01:22:46.127 --> 01:22:47.253
What?

1893
01:22:48.713 --> 01:22:49.923
What is it. Buzz?

1894
01:22:49.965 --> 01:22:51.675
Just listen to me.

1895
01:22:51.716 --> 01:22:53.176
I... I've been trying
to ask you this. and if...

1896
01:22:53.218 --> 01:22:55.637
if I don't do it now.
I never will.

1897
01:22:55.679 --> 01:22:58.139
-[♪ romantic music plays]
-Will you...

1898
01:22:58.181 --> 01:23:00.433
Buzz. you can do this.

1899
01:23:00.475 --> 01:23:01.851
Will... Will...

1900
01:23:04.896 --> 01:23:05.939
[gasps]

1901
01:23:07.941 --> 01:23:10.318
You're stuck with me. Deputy.

1902
01:23:15.991 --> 01:23:17.909
Cheer up. boys.
She'll be back.

1903
01:23:17.951 --> 01:23:19.828
We have a plan!

1904
01:23:19.869 --> 01:23:22.539
At ease. Ranger. At ease.

1905
01:23:22.580 --> 01:23:23.498
[music ends]

1906
01:23:29.212 --> 01:23:30.922
[♪ somber music plays]

1907
01:23:38.596 --> 01:23:40.098
[whirring]

1908
01:23:43.101 --> 01:23:44.602
Men. you know your mission.

1909
01:23:44.644 --> 01:23:45.645
Yes. Commander.

1910
01:23:46.521 --> 01:23:47.731
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

1911
01:23:50.233 --> 01:23:51.526
Woody! Buzz!

1912
01:23:51.568 --> 01:23:53.028
-What?
-[Rex] Lily!

1913
01:23:53.069 --> 01:23:54.529
-Oh. no. no. no.
-Foul device.

1914
01:23:54.571 --> 01:23:56.031
What's she doing here?

1915
01:23:56.072 --> 01:23:57.407
She's one of us. guys.
Deal with it.

1916
01:23:57.449 --> 01:23:58.992
Listen up. everyone.

1917
01:23:59.034 --> 01:24:00.702
Lily and Jessie
have a plan to help Bonnie.

1918
01:24:00.744 --> 01:24:02.537
Okay.
what do you need us to do?

1919
01:24:02.579 --> 01:24:03.705
Nothing.

1920
01:24:03.747 --> 01:24:05.373
-Nothing?
-That's easy.

1921
01:24:05.415 --> 01:24:07.083
Jessie already did
the hard work.

1922
01:24:07.125 --> 01:24:08.793
Classic Jessica.

1923
01:24:08.835 --> 01:24:11.379
All that's left for me
is to send a message.

1924
01:24:13.131 --> 01:24:14.257
[whirring]

1925
01:24:14.299 --> 01:24:16.092
[♪ happy music plays]

1926
01:24:26.019 --> 01:24:27.312
[grunts]

1927
01:24:29.355 --> 01:24:31.149
It's up to the girls now.

1928
01:24:31.983 --> 01:24:33.193
[yawns]

1929
01:24:33.985 --> 01:24:35.028
[music continues]

1930
01:24:39.699 --> 01:24:41.201
[gasps]

1931
01:24:44.954 --> 01:24:46.498
[giggles]

1932
01:24:51.920 --> 01:24:54.464
Hey. sweetie.
Look what I found in the car.

1933
01:24:54.506 --> 01:24:55.965
[gasps]

1934
01:24:56.007 --> 01:24:57.634
It's okay.
We turned off the chat.

1935
01:24:57.675 --> 01:24:59.344
[♪ somber music plays]

1936
01:25:06.601 --> 01:25:08.103
[doorbell rings]

1937
01:25:14.359 --> 01:25:16.736
Bonnie.
You have a friend at the door.

1938
01:25:16.778 --> 01:25:17.695
[gasps]

1939
01:25:18.738 --> 01:25:20.323
- Let's try to beat...
- Hi. Bonnie.

1940
01:25:20.365 --> 01:25:22.242
- ...our high score.
-I brought your dolls.

1941
01:25:23.952 --> 01:25:25.703
Bonnie. come say hi.

1942
01:25:25.745 --> 01:25:26.830
Okay.

1943
01:25:35.380 --> 01:25:36.464
Hi.

1944
01:25:37.257 --> 01:25:38.299
Hi.

1945
01:25:46.015 --> 01:25:47.934
I'm sorry.
I don't play with toys--

1946
01:25:47.976 --> 01:25:49.686
I played with her
a little yesterday.

1947
01:25:50.478 --> 01:25:52.021
I like it when she's like.

1948
01:25:52.063 --> 01:25:54.023
"I ain't afraid of nothin'.
partner."

1949
01:25:57.944 --> 01:25:58.987
[chuckles]

1950
01:26:00.697 --> 01:26:02.782
That... That was weird.

1951
01:26:03.241 --> 01:26:04.826
Uh... I...

1952
01:26:05.451 --> 01:26:06.578
Sorry I bothered you.

1953
01:26:11.541 --> 01:26:13.209
-Oh. no. Don't go.
-No. no. no.

1954
01:26:13.251 --> 01:26:14.669
-She can't go. She can't go.
-No. no. no. no.

1955
01:26:16.546 --> 01:26:17.630
Blaze!

1956
01:26:31.144 --> 01:26:34.272
I like your boots.

1957
01:26:37.817 --> 01:26:40.111
I... I really like your socks.

1958
01:26:42.780 --> 01:26:45.617
Do you like my beard. madame?

1959
01:26:46.284 --> 01:26:48.953
Very impressive. m'lady.

1960
01:26:48.995 --> 01:26:51.664
Yes.
I'm one billion years old.

1961
01:26:51.706 --> 01:26:53.750
That's why it's so glorious.

1962
01:26:57.879 --> 01:26:59.547
[Bonnie and Blaze laughing]

1963
01:27:01.424 --> 01:27:02.717
Um...

1964
01:27:02.759 --> 01:27:04.385
Do you wanna play?

1965
01:27:04.886 --> 01:27:05.929
[gasps]

1966
01:27:06.763 --> 01:27:07.805
Okay.

1967
01:27:08.848 --> 01:27:10.225
-Walter. let's go.
-Okay. Okay.

1968
01:27:10.266 --> 01:27:12.101
-Do you actually have a horse?
-Yeah.

1969
01:27:12.143 --> 01:27:13.603
[Bonnie] Like. a real one?

1970
01:27:13.645 --> 01:27:15.230
[Blaze laughs] Yes! It's real.

1971
01:27:17.857 --> 01:27:20.401
[gasps] Hey. I have an idea.

1972
01:27:20.443 --> 01:27:21.861
[♪ ceremonial music plays]

1973
01:27:22.820 --> 01:27:24.322
[chattering]

1974
01:27:28.409 --> 01:27:29.452
-[door opens]
-[gasping]

1975
01:27:29.494 --> 01:27:30.870
[gasping. clamoring]

1976
01:27:30.912 --> 01:27:32.538
[Dolly] Look at that kilt.

1977
01:27:33.998 --> 01:27:35.250
[gasps]

1978
01:27:38.169 --> 01:27:40.296
[blusters. cries]

1979
01:27:41.714 --> 01:27:43.216
[sniffling]

1980
01:27:43.258 --> 01:27:45.802
Please. take care of my son.

1981
01:27:49.305 --> 01:27:50.723
[clears throat]

1982
01:27:50.765 --> 01:27:53.810
Friends.
we are gathered here today

1983
01:27:53.851 --> 01:27:57.105
to witness
the most wonderfulest union

1984
01:27:57.146 --> 01:27:58.523
of Sheriff Jessie

1985
01:27:58.564 --> 01:28:01.276
and Buzz-tholomew
MacLightyear.

1986
01:28:01.317 --> 01:28:03.027
-[creaks]
-[beeping]

1987
01:28:09.367 --> 01:28:11.119
Now. Sheriff.

1988
01:28:11.160 --> 01:28:14.497
please put this ring
onto Buzz's itty-bitty finger

1989
01:28:14.539 --> 01:28:16.374
and make your vows.

1990
01:28:17.834 --> 01:28:20.378
Buzz. will you take this ring

1991
01:28:20.420 --> 01:28:22.088
as my pinky promise

1992
01:28:22.130 --> 01:28:25.133
to have fun.
and play with you and stuff.

1993
01:28:25.174 --> 01:28:27.093
for all my days.

1994
01:28:27.135 --> 01:28:29.137
even the hard ones?

1995
01:28:29.178 --> 01:28:31.764
-I do--
-[Bonnie's mom] Bonnie...

1996
01:28:31.806 --> 01:28:33.308
have you seen my wedding ring?

1997
01:28:33.349 --> 01:28:34.434
-[gasps]
-[giggles]

1998
01:28:34.475 --> 01:28:35.601
-[giggles]
-[shushes] Uh...

1999
01:28:35.643 --> 01:28:37.645
Maybe check the bathroom?

2000
01:28:37.687 --> 01:28:38.980
Wait. wait. wait.
We need. like...

2001
01:28:39.022 --> 01:28:40.231
Flowers! From the garden.

2002
01:28:40.273 --> 01:28:42.317
-Good idea.
-Follow me.

2003
01:28:42.358 --> 01:28:44.485
And there's confetti
in the craft drawer.

2004
01:28:45.570 --> 01:28:47.030
Oh. congrats. you two.

2005
01:28:47.071 --> 01:28:48.448
Don't worry.
I took plenty of photos

2006
01:28:48.489 --> 01:28:49.907
for Smarty and the gang.

2007
01:28:49.949 --> 01:28:52.368
That's really sweet of you.
Lily.

2008
01:28:52.910 --> 01:28:53.953
[chuckles]

2009
01:28:53.995 --> 01:28:54.912
Mmm.

2010
01:28:55.580 --> 01:28:57.040
You done good. Sheriff.

2011
01:28:57.790 --> 01:28:59.625
You can call me Jessica.

2012
01:29:00.251 --> 01:29:01.878
Okay. I will. Jessica.

2013
01:29:02.587 --> 01:29:04.088
Actually. no. No.

2014
